1
00:00:19,780 --> 00:00:22,980
=Weekend Crush=

2
00:00:23,020 --> 00:00:25,740
(Tianjin)

3
00:00:25,780 --> 00:00:28,060
(Early July,
one month after the final confession)

4
00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:39,440
Why do you have flowers?

5
00:00:39,440 --> 00:00:40,200
Hello.

6
00:00:42,080 --> 00:00:43,160
They're for you.

7
00:00:44,320 --> 00:00:45,280
I'll carry that for you.

8
00:00:45,280 --> 00:00:45,880
Okay.

9
00:00:45,880 --> 00:00:48,600
These match what you wore that day.

10
00:00:49,120 --> 00:00:50,360
I remember that day.

11
00:00:50,360 --> 00:00:50,800
Yeah.

12
00:00:52,080 --> 00:00:52,840
You get in first.

13
00:00:52,840 --> 00:00:53,440
Okay.

14
00:00:54,020 --> 00:00:55,520
(Protects her head)

15
00:00:55,520 --> 00:00:56,320
Thanks.

16
00:00:58,280 --> 00:01:00,040
Thanks, babe.

17
00:01:03,360 --> 00:01:05,280
Your outfit looks so good today.

18
00:01:05,520 --> 00:01:06,280
So does yours.

19
00:01:06,280 --> 00:01:06,960
You planned this, didn't you?

20
00:01:06,960 --> 00:01:08,000
We're always matching.

21
00:01:08,160 --> 00:01:08,960
Yeah.

22
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:10,100
(Matching colors)

23
00:01:11,120 --> 00:01:12,120
Why are you smiling?

24
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:13,120
You look good.

25
00:01:17,940 --> 00:01:18,980
(Reaches out)

26
00:01:18,980 --> 00:01:20,140
(Takes his hand)

27
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:22,320
It's only been three days. Why so shy?

28
00:01:24,080 --> 00:01:25,280
Am I being shy?

29
00:01:25,440 --> 00:01:26,200
You're not.

30
00:01:26,460 --> 00:01:28,980
(Holds on tighter)

31
00:01:31,640 --> 00:01:32,560
Missed me?

32
00:01:32,880 --> 00:01:33,680
Yeah.

33
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:38,680
Yeah.

34
00:01:41,680 --> 00:01:43,040
A little stunned, huh?

35
00:01:52,540 --> 00:01:54,340
(Yiheng's POV)
Top-tier camerawork.

36
00:01:54,360 --> 00:01:55,360
Is it really that good?

37
00:01:55,360 --> 00:01:56,200
I'm scared.

38
00:01:56,440 --> 00:01:58,120
Whenever you say "top-tier camerawork",

39
00:01:58,680 --> 00:01:59,680
I get nervous.

40
00:02:00,880 --> 00:02:01,680
I'll hold it.

41
00:02:03,480 --> 00:02:05,400
(Kaiyi's POV)
How're you feeling today, handsome?

42
00:02:05,720 --> 00:02:08,080
As good as ever.

43
00:02:08,440 --> 00:02:10,040
What do you mean, "as good as ever"?

44
00:02:10,320 --> 00:02:11,640
What does that mean?

45
00:02:11,640 --> 00:02:16,080
I'm always happy whenever I see you.

46
00:02:16,080 --> 00:02:20,500
(Seeing you always makes me happy)

47
00:02:20,720 --> 00:02:23,280
See these two canvases over here?

48
00:02:23,280 --> 00:02:24,480
What's this?

49
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:28,440
Did you sketch these?

50
00:02:28,440 --> 00:02:29,860
(Sketches prepared in advance)
Just a rough sketch.

51
00:02:29,880 --> 00:02:32,040
Remember when we watched...

52
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:33,000
Fang and Yu Yang?

53
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:33,800
Yeah.

54
00:02:34,200 --> 00:02:35,120
I think we didn't try it

55
00:02:35,120 --> 00:02:36,240
mainly because I told you

56
00:02:36,240 --> 00:02:37,960
I was scared I'd make you look ugly.

57
00:02:37,960 --> 00:02:39,800
So I got some oil pastels.

58
00:02:39,800 --> 00:02:40,920
They're easier to use.

59
00:02:40,920 --> 00:02:42,000
Why are my ears

60
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:43,880
so much bigger than yours?

61
00:02:43,880 --> 00:02:45,640
Your ears are bigger than mine.

62
00:02:46,880 --> 00:02:48,640
The sketches are based on real life.

63
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:50,720
Then why's my face bigger too?

64
00:02:51,320 --> 00:02:52,240
I don't think it is.

65
00:02:52,240 --> 00:02:53,160
You don't?

66
00:02:53,160 --> 00:02:54,160
See for yourself.

67
00:02:54,500 --> 00:02:56,420
(Kaiyi, Yiheng)

68
00:02:56,680 --> 00:02:58,200
I'll fix it for you later.

69
00:02:58,200 --> 00:02:59,760
Don't. It looks pretty good.

70
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:00,960
I'm just teasing you.

71
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:06,920
Today's also Fang and Yu Yang's

72
00:03:06,920 --> 00:03:07,880
anniversary.

73
00:03:07,880 --> 00:03:08,920
Yeah.

74
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:10,200
Wonder what they're up to.

75
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:11,200
Yeah.

76
00:03:11,200 --> 00:03:12,760
Meanwhile, elsewhere...

77
00:03:14,540 --> 00:03:17,140
(Meanwhile, elsewhere...)

78
00:03:19,440 --> 00:03:20,240
Time to eat!

79
00:03:21,080 --> 00:03:22,280
Time for me to eat!

80
00:03:22,420 --> 00:03:24,820
(A day apart, eating alone)

81
00:03:26,300 --> 00:03:29,020
(Video diary)

82
00:03:29,060 --> 00:03:34,820
(Yu Yang's super loyal sticky bean bun)

83
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:39,260
(Incoming call)

84
00:03:39,260 --> 00:03:41,420
(Smiles)

85
00:03:42,640 --> 00:03:43,440
Hello!

86
00:03:43,860 --> 00:03:45,380
(Yu Yang, on a work trip in Shenzhen)

87
00:03:47,440 --> 00:03:48,400
Look who it is.

88
00:03:48,400 --> 00:03:49,360
Do you recognize me?

89
00:03:50,040 --> 00:03:50,840
Miss me?

90
00:03:51,760 --> 00:03:53,200
(Misses him so much)
I miss you so much too.

91
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:55,720
I wish I could just teleport over.

92
00:03:56,320 --> 00:03:56,720
That fast?

93
00:03:56,720 --> 00:03:57,960
At 10PM, you're gonna

94
00:03:57,960 --> 00:03:59,720
see me at your door.

95
00:03:59,720 --> 00:04:01,000
(Just kidding)
You'll see me in the front row,

96
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:02,560
right in the middle.

97
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:04,320
That'd be amazing.

98
00:04:04,320 --> 00:04:05,280
I'd be so excited.

99
00:04:05,280 --> 00:04:06,840
But I think

100
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:08,560
it'd be pretty hard

101
00:04:08,560 --> 00:04:09,720
to fool you like that.

102
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:10,840
Because

103
00:04:10,840 --> 00:04:11,920
I'd have to fly over,

104
00:04:11,920 --> 00:04:13,360
so we couldn't talk for two hours.

105
00:04:13,360 --> 00:04:15,320
We rarely go two hours without talking.

106
00:04:15,320 --> 00:04:16,200
Yeah, that's true.

107
00:04:16,200 --> 00:04:17,560
That's how newlyweds are. Wait, no!

108
00:04:17,560 --> 00:04:18,560
No!

109
00:04:19,440 --> 00:04:20,600
What am I saying?

110
00:04:23,480 --> 00:04:23,920
Sorry.

111
00:04:23,920 --> 00:04:24,800
I'm talking nonsense.

112
00:04:26,440 --> 00:04:27,000
Cheers.

113
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:28,880
I'll toast you with my coffee.

114
00:04:34,060 --> 00:04:35,640
I don't even know where you are.

115
00:04:36,280 --> 00:04:37,480
You don't know where I am?

116
00:04:38,240 --> 00:04:39,760
I don't know which venue

117
00:04:39,760 --> 00:04:40,760
you're at.

118
00:04:41,040 --> 00:04:44,400
I can't order you some fruit.

119
00:04:45,680 --> 00:04:47,840
It's okay. I've got chili peppers here.

120
00:04:47,840 --> 00:04:48,400
Okay.

121
00:04:49,040 --> 00:04:49,840
Mukbang time.

122
00:04:49,840 --> 00:04:50,640
Here's mine.

123
00:04:52,040 --> 00:04:52,840
Mukbang time.

124
00:04:53,240 --> 00:04:54,040
Mukbang time.

125
00:04:56,600 --> 00:04:57,160
Who is it?

126
00:04:58,040 --> 00:04:58,840
Hold on.

127
00:05:02,160 --> 00:05:02,760
Hello.

128
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:03,720
Delivery for you.

129
00:05:03,900 --> 00:05:05,360
(Express delivery arrives)
For me?

130
00:05:05,360 --> 00:05:05,960
Yes.

131
00:05:05,960 --> 00:05:06,280
Thanks.

132
00:05:06,280 --> 00:05:07,120
Flowers too.

133
00:05:08,260 --> 00:05:09,860
(Smiles)
Okay.

134
00:05:13,080 --> 00:05:14,680
Did you hear the doorbell?

135
00:05:15,400 --> 00:05:16,480
Nope.

136
00:05:16,480 --> 00:05:17,300
(Playing dumb)

137
00:05:17,300 --> 00:05:18,280
(Smiles)

138
00:05:18,290 --> 00:05:20,800
Who sent me this?

139
00:05:22,080 --> 00:05:23,640
Who's sending you gifts?

140
00:05:25,180 --> 00:05:26,490
Oh my God!

141
00:05:27,240 --> 00:05:28,600
Did you send this to me, Sparkle?

142
00:05:28,600 --> 00:05:30,080
You're so good at gifts,

143
00:05:30,080 --> 00:05:31,000
Sparkle!

144
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:31,860
(Can't keep a straight face)

145
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:33,760
Show me who sent it.

146
00:05:33,760 --> 00:05:34,560
What'd you get?

147
00:05:35,080 --> 00:05:36,120
Who sent it?

148
00:05:36,120 --> 00:05:37,760
Someone whose last name is "Your".

149
00:05:40,160 --> 00:05:41,360
And their first name

150
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:42,760
is "Baby".

151
00:05:42,980 --> 00:05:47,100
(Last name: Your. First name: Baby)

152
00:05:52,120 --> 00:05:53,080
So?

153
00:05:53,080 --> 00:05:53,960
Like it?

154
00:05:53,960 --> 00:05:55,320
Know why I got it for you?

155
00:05:55,320 --> 00:05:56,160
One month!

156
00:05:57,090 --> 00:05:58,080
That's right.

157
00:05:58,320 --> 00:05:59,000
Hello.

158
00:06:00,120 --> 00:06:00,840
Hello.

159
00:06:00,840 --> 00:06:01,800
Happy one-month anniversary!

160
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:04,380
(Happy one-month anniversary)

161
00:06:04,640 --> 00:06:05,920
A mermaid.

162
00:06:05,920 --> 00:06:08,200
Yeah. Didn't you say you liked Barbies?

163
00:06:09,200 --> 00:06:10,080
Watch your hand.

164
00:06:10,560 --> 00:06:11,200
Okay.

165
00:06:11,200 --> 00:06:12,680
I'm a kid again.

166
00:06:12,680 --> 00:06:13,480
Sparkle,

167
00:06:14,480 --> 00:06:15,180
paw!

168
00:06:15,180 --> 00:06:17,040
(Laughs)

169
00:06:17,040 --> 00:06:18,840
Hug!

170
00:06:18,840 --> 00:06:20,720
Can you take a picture of us?

171
00:06:23,560 --> 00:06:24,200
Okay.

172
00:06:25,160 --> 00:06:26,800
Time flies.

173
00:06:26,800 --> 00:06:28,080
Seriously.

174
00:06:28,080 --> 00:06:30,160
I can't believe
it's already been a month.

175
00:06:30,600 --> 00:06:31,440
Yeah.

176
00:06:31,440 --> 00:06:33,680
I really wish I could be
with you in Beijing.

177
00:06:33,680 --> 00:06:36,440
(Spending their anniversary in two cities)
Our show just ends too late.

178
00:06:36,440 --> 00:06:38,000
Otherwise, I'd fly over

179
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:39,880
right after the show

180
00:06:39,880 --> 00:06:40,840
if there were a late flight.

181
00:06:41,640 --> 00:06:44,280
Don't push yourself. It's too tiring.

182
00:06:44,840 --> 00:06:48,720
We'll have to get used to this.

183
00:06:51,880 --> 00:06:54,440
We're both so clingy.

184
00:06:54,440 --> 00:06:55,480
We can't stay apart too long.

185
00:06:56,320 --> 00:06:57,760
At least I can't.

186
00:06:58,400 --> 00:06:59,920
I've noticed that whenever

187
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:02,040
we're apart for a while

188
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:03,720
and finally see each other again,

189
00:07:03,720 --> 00:07:04,640
it feels like...

190
00:07:05,600 --> 00:07:07,240
a sweet reunion.

191
00:07:07,880 --> 00:07:09,160
Absence makes the heart grow fonder.

192
00:07:09,480 --> 00:07:12,200
It's pretty amazing.

193
00:07:12,600 --> 00:07:13,760
Even my mom says...

194
00:07:16,160 --> 00:07:16,760
What?

195
00:07:16,760 --> 00:07:17,840
Whenever I go on a work trip,

196
00:07:18,780 --> 00:07:20,760
my mom's like,

197
00:07:20,760 --> 00:07:23,000
you're always traveling!

198
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:24,480
What about your girlfriend?

199
00:07:24,480 --> 00:07:25,760
You never spend time with her.

200
00:07:25,760 --> 00:07:26,680
What are you gonna do?

201
00:07:26,700 --> 00:07:28,700
(Laughs)

202
00:07:29,680 --> 00:07:32,320
But she doesn't know
we're always video calling.

203
00:07:33,080 --> 00:07:34,880
Now whenever she calls me,

204
00:07:35,280 --> 00:07:37,160
she always has to ask

205
00:07:37,160 --> 00:07:37,920
how you're doing.

206
00:07:39,480 --> 00:07:40,800
I gotta teleport back.

207
00:07:40,800 --> 00:07:42,960
See you tomorrow!

208
00:07:42,960 --> 00:07:43,720
I gotta go.

209
00:07:43,720 --> 00:07:45,920
I need to get ready.

210
00:07:45,920 --> 00:07:46,960
Okay, go ahead.

211
00:07:46,960 --> 00:07:48,280
I'm off!

212
00:07:49,800 --> 00:07:51,360
Bye!

213
00:08:04,460 --> 00:08:05,860
(Beijing)

214
00:08:05,880 --> 00:08:07,200
Hello!

215
00:08:07,760 --> 00:08:08,920
Happy birthday!

216
00:08:08,920 --> 00:08:09,760
Thanks!

217
00:08:09,860 --> 00:08:12,080
(Mid-July, Yue'er's birthday)

218
00:08:12,080 --> 00:08:13,000
Miss me?

219
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:13,800
I did.

220
00:08:14,080 --> 00:08:15,240
I missed you too.

221
00:08:15,840 --> 00:08:16,800
You look handsome today.

222
00:08:16,800 --> 00:08:17,800
(Compliments)
You look beautiful today.

223
00:08:18,520 --> 00:08:19,200
Hop in.

224
00:08:19,200 --> 00:08:20,080
Let's go.

225
00:08:20,620 --> 00:08:21,360
(Opens the door)

226
00:08:21,360 --> 00:08:22,160
Thanks!

227
00:08:23,040 --> 00:08:24,600
I loosened the water bottle cap for you.

228
00:08:24,600 --> 00:08:26,160
(So thoughtful)
Awesome. Oh my God.

229
00:08:27,040 --> 00:08:28,880
(Xilun's POV)
Hello!

230
00:08:28,880 --> 00:08:30,960
Today is Yue'er's...

231
00:08:30,960 --> 00:08:32,560
It's my first birthday with her.

232
00:08:32,560 --> 00:08:33,800
It's her 22nd birthday.

233
00:08:33,800 --> 00:08:34,600
That's right.

234
00:08:36,840 --> 00:08:38,120
It's tracking you.

235
00:08:38,120 --> 00:08:38,960
See? You're the star.

236
00:08:38,960 --> 00:08:40,720
It can't even recognize my face.

237
00:08:40,720 --> 00:08:42,960
Even when I'm here, it turns to you.

238
00:08:42,960 --> 00:08:44,200
Because you're the star.

239
00:08:44,200 --> 00:08:45,240
I already gave it

240
00:08:45,240 --> 00:08:46,280
special instructions.

241
00:08:48,240 --> 00:08:48,760
Okay.

242
00:08:50,880 --> 00:08:52,120
Let's go eat.

243
00:08:52,680 --> 00:08:54,720
How's your birthday going?

244
00:08:55,080 --> 00:08:56,000
It's not...

245
00:08:56,160 --> 00:08:57,000
(Yue'er's POV)
It hasn't happened yet.

246
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:57,800
Yeah!

247
00:08:58,240 --> 00:08:59,720
How was your birthday yesterday?

248
00:08:59,920 --> 00:09:01,240
I had a great time yesterday.

249
00:09:01,720 --> 00:09:03,200
What about this afternoon?

250
00:09:03,200 --> 00:09:04,680
That was pretty fun too.

251
00:09:04,680 --> 00:09:06,440
Do I sound like
your elementary school teacher?

252
00:09:06,660 --> 00:09:08,000
(Laughs)

253
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:09,960
(Yue'er's POV)
Like I'm helping you write an essay.

254
00:09:14,980 --> 00:09:19,820
(Yue'er's POV,
arriving at the restaurant)

255
00:09:19,860 --> 00:09:21,260
(Xilun's POV)

256
00:09:21,480 --> 00:09:22,880
You've even got a spotlight.

257
00:09:22,880 --> 00:09:24,800
Because you're the moon goddess.

258
00:09:25,380 --> 00:09:26,960
(Xilun's POV)
I love you.

259
00:09:26,960 --> 00:09:27,960
I "hate" you.

260
00:09:30,720 --> 00:09:32,800
Can we get a mosquito's-eye view?

261
00:09:36,360 --> 00:09:36,880
Bottoms up.

262
00:09:36,880 --> 00:09:37,280
Cheers!

263
00:09:37,560 --> 00:09:38,320
I'm drinking it all!

264
00:09:39,800 --> 00:09:40,600
Cheers!

265
00:09:44,640 --> 00:09:45,600
Is your hand feeling any better?

266
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:46,580
(Concerned)
You don't need to support it anymore.

267
00:09:46,580 --> 00:09:47,840
I heal fast, babe.

268
00:09:49,920 --> 00:09:51,040
I've only got one good hand.

269
00:09:51,040 --> 00:09:52,040
How am I gonna cut this?

270
00:09:53,120 --> 00:09:54,160
I'll cut it for you.

271
00:09:54,160 --> 00:09:55,960
Can you hold it with your fork?

272
00:09:55,960 --> 00:09:56,760
Sure.

273
00:09:58,400 --> 00:09:59,040
So pretty.

274
00:10:00,160 --> 00:10:01,320
Wanna make a wish?

275
00:10:01,320 --> 00:10:01,600
Yeah.

276
00:10:01,600 --> 00:10:02,760
Close your eyes and make a wish.

277
00:10:02,760 --> 00:10:03,400
Okay.

278
00:10:07,480 --> 00:10:08,320
Done!

279
00:10:08,320 --> 00:10:09,120
Okay.

280
00:10:09,580 --> 00:10:14,300
(LunYue Full Moon)

281
00:10:14,480 --> 00:10:16,880
(Xilun's POV)
I finally get to give you red flowers.

282
00:10:16,880 --> 00:10:18,320
Back at the Signal House,

283
00:10:18,320 --> 00:10:19,120
I always thought

284
00:10:19,120 --> 00:10:21,240
red flowers were a bit too forward.

285
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:24,000
I didn't know you liked roses either.

286
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:25,400
When you told me

287
00:10:25,400 --> 00:10:26,440
you liked jasmine,

288
00:10:26,440 --> 00:10:28,560
I thought you preferred white flowers.

289
00:10:29,080 --> 00:10:30,760
So I kept getting you white ones.

290
00:10:30,760 --> 00:10:32,440
There's even a white one in the middle.

291
00:10:32,440 --> 00:10:33,080
Yes.

292
00:10:33,080 --> 00:10:35,440
I hope we'll always be happy together.

293
00:10:35,440 --> 00:10:37,600
And I hope you're happy every day.

294
00:10:37,600 --> 00:10:38,800
That's so thoughtful.

295
00:10:38,800 --> 00:10:39,840
Red represents love.

296
00:10:39,840 --> 00:10:41,560
And the white one's surrounded by it.

297
00:10:41,560 --> 00:10:42,920
(Red represents love,
with you surrounded by it)

298
00:10:42,920 --> 00:10:44,480
So that's what it means!

299
00:10:45,640 --> 00:10:47,680
We'll have amazing birthdays together
from now on.

300
00:10:47,880 --> 00:10:49,320
Amazing!

301
00:10:49,640 --> 00:10:50,920
Go ahead and open it.

302
00:10:51,440 --> 00:10:52,720
What's this?

303
00:10:52,940 --> 00:10:54,260
(A gift)

304
00:10:55,120 --> 00:10:56,400
You know what's funny?

305
00:10:56,400 --> 00:10:58,600
I've wanted to get you these for ages.

306
00:11:05,940 --> 00:11:07,740
(Glasses)

307
00:11:08,320 --> 00:11:09,360
Are they prescription?

308
00:11:09,360 --> 00:11:10,440
No, we'll need to get lenses.

309
00:11:10,440 --> 00:11:12,240
We can go get them fitted together.

310
00:11:14,160 --> 00:11:15,200
Remember how you kept saying

311
00:11:15,200 --> 00:11:16,400
you wanted new glasses?

312
00:11:16,920 --> 00:11:18,000
And I remembered how good

313
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:19,880
you looked in mine.

314
00:11:19,880 --> 00:11:20,800
So practical.

315
00:11:20,800 --> 00:11:21,760
Very practical.

316
00:11:23,360 --> 00:11:25,280
And I know these will look great on you.

317
00:11:27,720 --> 00:11:29,000
They do look pretty good.

318
00:11:29,560 --> 00:11:30,120
Right?

319
00:11:30,120 --> 00:11:31,320
Yeah, not bad.

320
00:11:31,320 --> 00:11:33,200
Thank you!

321
00:11:35,420 --> 00:11:37,860
(Late July, a weekend off)

322
00:11:39,600 --> 00:11:41,720
Hello, Yihang!

323
00:11:41,720 --> 00:11:42,320
You're here?

324
00:11:43,560 --> 00:11:44,000
Hop in.

325
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:44,800
I'll put this in the back.

326
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:50,000
How've you been?

327
00:11:50,720 --> 00:11:51,640
Pretty good.

328
00:11:51,640 --> 00:11:52,200
Busy?

329
00:11:52,720 --> 00:11:53,600
Not too bad.

330
00:11:53,600 --> 00:11:55,440
Just the usual.

331
00:11:55,440 --> 00:11:56,840
You seemed pretty busy lately.

332
00:11:56,840 --> 00:11:58,600
Yeah, I just finished up.

333
00:11:58,600 --> 00:11:59,520
Just got out of a meeting.

334
00:12:01,780 --> 00:12:02,940
(Reunited after days apart)

335
00:12:03,160 --> 00:12:03,800
It's been too long.

336
00:12:03,800 --> 00:12:04,720
I kinda missed you.

337
00:12:05,160 --> 00:12:06,000
Of course.

338
00:12:06,680 --> 00:12:08,400
You look pretty handsome today.

339
00:12:08,400 --> 00:12:09,280
You too.

340
00:12:09,920 --> 00:12:11,520
New look today, Yihang?

341
00:12:11,520 --> 00:12:13,000
Nah, my hair's just longer.

342
00:12:13,890 --> 00:12:15,480
I'll message
the girls in the group chat.

343
00:12:15,480 --> 00:12:16,760
Let them know we're on our way.

344
00:12:16,760 --> 00:12:17,400
Sure.

345
00:12:19,600 --> 00:12:22,080
(One big happy family (4))
Yihang and I just met up.

346
00:12:22,080 --> 00:12:24,880
We're heading over to you two now.

347
00:12:29,920 --> 00:12:31,920
Did you sleep well last night?

348
00:12:32,680 --> 00:12:33,560
I was a little excited.

349
00:12:33,560 --> 00:12:34,520
Excited, huh?

350
00:12:34,520 --> 00:12:36,280
Yeah, I couldn't wait.

351
00:12:37,160 --> 00:12:38,600
It's nice that all four of us

352
00:12:38,600 --> 00:12:39,520
get to hang out together.

353
00:12:39,790 --> 00:12:40,520
Yeah.

354
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:44,160
Almost there.

355
00:12:44,160 --> 00:12:45,080
We're right outside.

356
00:12:49,520 --> 00:12:50,040
Hey, guys!

357
00:12:50,040 --> 00:12:50,840
Hello!

358
00:12:51,880 --> 00:12:52,600
Here.

359
00:12:52,600 --> 00:12:53,880
Let me carry that.

360
00:12:53,880 --> 00:12:54,720
(Both reach for it)
Sure.

361
00:12:54,720 --> 00:12:56,720
You brought food too?

362
00:12:56,720 --> 00:12:57,680
Just a little.

363
00:12:57,680 --> 00:12:59,160
Got everything you need, right?

364
00:12:59,840 --> 00:13:00,400
Yep.

365
00:13:00,760 --> 00:13:01,200
Okay.

366
00:13:01,200 --> 00:13:02,360
A little mouse stole it.

367
00:13:02,800 --> 00:13:03,400
Okay.

368
00:13:05,920 --> 00:13:07,440
I'll put this in the trunk.

369
00:13:07,960 --> 00:13:08,840
What's this supposed to mean?

370
00:13:11,470 --> 00:13:13,280
What? What's wrong? Tell me.

371
00:13:13,280 --> 00:13:14,120
Nothing.

372
00:13:14,120 --> 00:13:14,840
What's up?

373
00:13:14,840 --> 00:13:15,760
Nothing.

374
00:13:15,760 --> 00:13:17,040
You say it's nothing...

375
00:13:17,040 --> 00:13:17,440
Then you two...

376
00:13:17,440 --> 00:13:19,120
Si can ride shotgun, right?

377
00:13:19,120 --> 00:13:19,500
Sure.

378
00:13:19,500 --> 00:13:20,250
(All planned out)
Yihang's driving.

379
00:13:20,250 --> 00:13:20,960
I'll take that.

380
00:13:20,960 --> 00:13:21,920
I'll put it in the car.

381
00:13:21,920 --> 00:13:24,100
(Opens the door for her)
Okay, let's go.

382
00:13:30,020 --> 00:13:32,260
(Laughs)

383
00:13:33,880 --> 00:13:34,720
We're off.

384
00:13:37,160 --> 00:13:38,800
Have some fruit.

385
00:13:39,280 --> 00:13:40,400
Yihang, want some fruit?

386
00:13:40,400 --> 00:13:41,500
(Imitating her)

387
00:13:42,520 --> 00:13:43,840
So, are you happy today?

388
00:13:43,840 --> 00:13:44,880
I'm pretty happy.

389
00:13:44,880 --> 00:13:45,840
Why?

390
00:13:46,360 --> 00:13:48,560
Because I get to see you.

391
00:13:48,560 --> 00:13:50,300
(Because I get to see you)

392
00:13:51,060 --> 00:13:52,860
(Smiles)

393
00:13:59,740 --> 00:14:01,620
(Brushes her hair aside)

394
00:14:01,640 --> 00:14:04,760
Is your hair getting in your eyes?

395
00:14:04,760 --> 00:14:05,560
Does it bother you?

396
00:14:06,040 --> 00:14:06,600
Not really.

397
00:14:08,300 --> 00:14:11,020
(Stares)

398
00:14:13,940 --> 00:14:15,700
(Smiles shyly)

399
00:14:21,940 --> 00:14:23,300
(Glances)

400
00:14:23,900 --> 00:14:25,340
(Smiles)

401
00:14:28,200 --> 00:14:29,440
This thing...

402
00:14:31,700 --> 00:14:32,700
(Checks)

403
00:14:34,650 --> 00:14:35,880
Wanna put that down?

404
00:14:36,860 --> 00:14:37,800
(Pulls)

405
00:14:37,800 --> 00:14:39,520
What if I sit here?

406
00:14:39,520 --> 00:14:40,800
(Wants to sit closer)
Wouldn't that be uncomfortable?

407
00:14:40,800 --> 00:14:41,720
Would it?

408
00:14:41,720 --> 00:14:42,680
Not really.

409
00:14:43,400 --> 00:14:44,080
Know why?

410
00:14:44,080 --> 00:14:45,920
There's this little headrest.

411
00:14:45,920 --> 00:14:46,640
It's pretty comfy to lean on.

412
00:14:46,640 --> 00:14:48,120
Is there a seat belt there?

413
00:14:48,120 --> 00:14:49,000
Yeah, there is.

414
00:14:49,180 --> 00:14:51,540
(Moves closer)

415
00:14:59,240 --> 00:15:00,680
Know why I like sitting here?

416
00:15:00,680 --> 00:15:01,120
Why?

417
00:15:01,120 --> 00:15:01,560
Because...

418
00:15:01,560 --> 00:15:02,280
It's against your head.

419
00:15:02,280 --> 00:15:04,040
Yeah, it's actually really comfy.

420
00:15:04,040 --> 00:15:05,920
If this were a little higher...

421
00:15:05,920 --> 00:15:07,200
This is perfect for my height.

422
00:15:07,200 --> 00:15:08,480
My head rests right here.

423
00:15:08,480 --> 00:15:09,640
It's pretty comfortable.

424
00:15:14,580 --> 00:15:16,300
(Si's POV)

425
00:15:16,320 --> 00:15:17,400
We're almost there.

426
00:15:18,560 --> 00:15:19,640
Adorable Si.

427
00:15:20,760 --> 00:15:22,680
Say that again.

428
00:15:22,680 --> 00:15:24,900
(Si's POV)
I said Si's super cute.

429
00:15:24,920 --> 00:15:27,080
I've never seen her with this hairstyle.

430
00:15:27,760 --> 00:15:30,120
Those little wispy bangs
suit her perfectly.

431
00:15:30,360 --> 00:15:31,320
Really?

432
00:15:31,800 --> 00:15:33,320
That hairstyle really suits you.

433
00:15:33,320 --> 00:15:34,040
Really?

434
00:15:34,040 --> 00:15:36,400
(Si's POV)
I think it's your best look yet.

435
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:38,760
You're making that up.

436
00:15:38,760 --> 00:15:39,240
Seriously.

437
00:15:39,240 --> 00:15:39,720
Seriously?

438
00:15:40,280 --> 00:15:41,560
Can you tell when I'm lying

439
00:15:41,560 --> 00:15:42,640
or telling the truth?

440
00:15:42,640 --> 00:15:43,400
Of course.

441
00:15:43,400 --> 00:15:44,520
Was I telling the truth?

442
00:15:44,520 --> 00:15:45,040
Yes.

443
00:15:45,040 --> 00:15:46,360
Because I think so too.

444
00:15:47,740 --> 00:15:49,420
(Bursts out laughing)

445
00:15:54,480 --> 00:15:55,200
We're here.

446
00:16:00,280 --> 00:16:00,920
We can even pick mushrooms.

447
00:16:01,400 --> 00:16:02,640
These little fishes are gold.

448
00:16:03,840 --> 00:16:04,960
The cooking area.

449
00:16:05,600 --> 00:16:06,320
This is where we cook.

450
00:16:06,320 --> 00:16:07,120
Right here.

451
00:16:07,600 --> 00:16:09,250
This is our craft workshop.

452
00:16:09,250 --> 00:16:10,200
(Pottery, tie-dye, plants, fabrics)
The crafting area.

453
00:16:10,200 --> 00:16:11,000
For tie-dye.

454
00:16:11,240 --> 00:16:12,480
We can make pottery here?

455
00:16:12,480 --> 00:16:13,280
Yep.

456
00:16:13,560 --> 00:16:14,920
That's the terrarium area.

457
00:16:15,360 --> 00:16:16,320
Wanna make a terrarium?

458
00:16:16,320 --> 00:16:17,520
I wanna make this.

459
00:16:17,520 --> 00:16:18,720
(Si and Yihang choose pottery)

460
00:16:18,720 --> 00:16:19,960
Let's make mini terrariums.

461
00:16:20,140 --> 00:16:20,960
(Xing and Bohan choose mini terrariums)

462
00:16:20,960 --> 00:16:22,240
Let's split up for now.

463
00:16:22,240 --> 00:16:22,840
You guys... We'll...

464
00:16:22,840 --> 00:16:23,640
You guys do this first.

465
00:16:23,640 --> 00:16:24,240
We'll do that first.

466
00:16:24,240 --> 00:16:24,560
Sure.

467
00:16:24,560 --> 00:16:25,200
Sounds good.

468
00:16:27,080 --> 00:16:29,000
(Bohan's POV)
Let's make a little terrarium.

469
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:30,160
When you were sick,

470
00:16:30,960 --> 00:16:32,520
I made a little round one.

471
00:16:33,840 --> 00:16:35,400
(This is my second letter to Xing)
That afternoon, I went alone

472
00:16:35,400 --> 00:16:37,080
(Xing, you said you love walking in gardens)
to the Dong Siying flower market.

473
00:16:37,440 --> 00:16:39,480
(watching greenery sway in the breeze)
The scent of flowers filled the bustling market.

474
00:16:39,920 --> 00:16:41,160
I wandered around for ages.

475
00:16:41,160 --> 00:16:42,840
Finally, I picked out

476
00:16:43,240 --> 00:16:44,440
a little terrarium.

477
00:16:46,320 --> 00:16:47,360
How about this?

478
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:49,260
Let's make one for each other.

479
00:16:49,260 --> 00:16:49,800
(Making one for each other)
Sure.

480
00:16:49,800 --> 00:16:50,600
- Sound good?
- Yeah.

481
00:16:51,880 --> 00:16:52,360
Careful.

482
00:16:52,360 --> 00:16:53,480
Don't get it on your dress.

483
00:16:53,480 --> 00:16:54,300
(Concerned)

484
00:16:59,600 --> 00:17:01,120
You missed a spot down here.

485
00:17:01,120 --> 00:17:01,900
(Points it out)

486
00:17:03,880 --> 00:17:05,440
This takes a steady hand.

487
00:17:05,640 --> 00:17:06,320
Yeah.

488
00:17:06,320 --> 00:17:07,400
Do you usually

489
00:17:07,400 --> 00:17:09,200
enjoy this kind of detailed work?

490
00:17:09,440 --> 00:17:10,400
I rarely do it.

491
00:17:10,920 --> 00:17:12,440
But it's pretty fun.

492
00:17:13,140 --> 00:17:14,820
(Glances)

493
00:17:15,080 --> 00:17:16,200
Yours looks really nice.

494
00:17:16,560 --> 00:17:17,880
(Compliments)
Yours looks great too.

495
00:17:20,700 --> 00:17:21,480
(Making cups)

496
00:17:21,480 --> 00:17:22,440
I'll make you a cup

497
00:17:22,440 --> 00:17:24,360
that's perfect for your tiny mouth.

498
00:17:24,720 --> 00:17:26,780
Then I'll make one that's
perfect for you.

499
00:17:26,780 --> 00:17:28,380
(Making cups for each other)

500
00:17:31,520 --> 00:17:33,120
Flatten out any sharp edges.

501
00:17:33,120 --> 00:17:34,920
Yeah, just make it round.

502
00:17:35,080 --> 00:17:36,160
Straight down.

503
00:17:36,360 --> 00:17:37,040
Yeah.

504
00:17:37,520 --> 00:17:38,460
(Glances)
Yeah.

505
00:17:39,040 --> 00:17:39,540
Yeah.

506
00:17:39,540 --> 00:17:40,740
(Lends a hand)

507
00:17:45,340 --> 00:17:46,420
(Takes it)

508
00:17:48,520 --> 00:17:49,200
It's a little tall.

509
00:17:49,200 --> 00:17:49,840
I'll press it down.

510
00:17:50,080 --> 00:17:51,320
I'll smooth it out for you.

511
00:17:51,320 --> 00:17:52,040
(Helps out)

512
00:17:52,040 --> 00:17:52,680
Yours...

513
00:17:53,440 --> 00:17:54,720
Yours is already so smooth?

514
00:17:54,720 --> 00:17:55,680
Yeah, mine...

515
00:17:56,320 --> 00:17:57,580
You've got a knack for this.

516
00:17:57,580 --> 00:17:58,340
(Compliments)

517
00:18:02,280 --> 00:18:04,000
We can drink from these someday.

518
00:18:04,280 --> 00:18:05,600
Then I'd better make yours sturdier.

519
00:18:05,600 --> 00:18:07,940
(Changes the design)
This shape doesn't look very sturdy.

520
00:18:10,640 --> 00:18:12,540
Use this side when you wanna drink fast.

521
00:18:12,540 --> 00:18:13,180
(For big gulps)

522
00:18:14,120 --> 00:18:15,540
And this side when you wanna sip.

523
00:18:15,540 --> 00:18:16,060
(Small sips)

524
00:18:16,100 --> 00:18:17,380
(Waiting for praise)

525
00:18:18,120 --> 00:18:19,560
What's the difference?

526
00:18:21,520 --> 00:18:22,640
The water flows differently.

527
00:18:22,740 --> 00:18:23,940
(Flow rate)

528
00:18:24,080 --> 00:18:26,040
(Clever design)
This side has a wider opening.

529
00:18:26,040 --> 00:18:26,840
This one's narrower.

530
00:18:29,880 --> 00:18:30,600
Look.

531
00:18:30,600 --> 00:18:31,620
I'll give you three sides.

532
00:18:31,620 --> 00:18:32,180
(Another bright idea)

533
00:18:32,320 --> 00:18:33,880
Use this one for medium sips.

534
00:18:33,900 --> 00:18:34,960
(Medium sips?)

535
00:18:34,960 --> 00:18:36,240
So it's a triangle?

536
00:18:36,240 --> 00:18:36,680
Yeah.

537
00:18:36,680 --> 00:18:37,960
I thought you were making a heart.

538
00:18:37,960 --> 00:18:38,960
Yeah, it is a heart.

539
00:18:43,080 --> 00:18:44,280
We can write on the side.

540
00:18:45,040 --> 00:18:46,760
What are you gonna write?

541
00:18:46,760 --> 00:18:47,600
I'll write...

542
00:18:48,760 --> 00:18:49,960
"Hope you live to 100".

543
00:18:51,360 --> 00:18:52,680
Just write "Live to 100".

544
00:18:53,160 --> 00:18:53,960
Sound good?

545
00:18:55,280 --> 00:18:56,080
Sure.

546
00:18:58,920 --> 00:19:00,520
Why does it look like a mouse?

547
00:19:00,540 --> 00:19:02,220
(Mouse-shaped design)

548
00:19:05,040 --> 00:19:06,080
What did you say?

549
00:19:06,220 --> 00:19:08,340
(Cracks up)

550
00:19:10,320 --> 00:19:11,120
What is it?

551
00:19:11,980 --> 00:19:13,500
(Laughs)

552
00:19:13,760 --> 00:19:14,560
What is it?

553
00:19:14,560 --> 00:19:17,400
I keep thinking about you saying

554
00:19:17,400 --> 00:19:18,860
(Can't stop laughing)
that yours looks like a mouse.

555
00:19:22,320 --> 00:19:24,240
Know why it looks like a mouse?

556
00:19:24,240 --> 00:19:25,040
Why?

557
00:19:25,760 --> 00:19:28,000
Because cup handles are usually here.

558
00:19:28,920 --> 00:19:29,520
Over here?

559
00:19:29,520 --> 00:19:31,200
Yeah, from that angle...

560
00:19:31,400 --> 00:19:32,320
How about two handles?

561
00:19:32,980 --> 00:19:34,760
(Speechless)

562
00:19:34,760 --> 00:19:35,280
Two handles.

563
00:19:35,280 --> 00:19:36,520
I'll give you two handles.

564
00:19:36,520 --> 00:19:37,200
Unique, right?

565
00:19:38,440 --> 00:19:40,160
You can put the other handle here.

566
00:19:40,160 --> 00:19:41,440
You've already got a heart.

567
00:19:41,880 --> 00:19:42,840
Which hand do you drink with?

568
00:19:43,920 --> 00:19:44,720
My right.

569
00:19:45,300 --> 00:19:47,940
(Handles on both sides)

570
00:19:49,180 --> 00:19:50,980
(Looks around)

571
00:19:51,280 --> 00:19:52,400
What do you need?

572
00:19:52,640 --> 00:19:53,540
Here's one.

573
00:19:53,540 --> 00:19:54,820
(Hands it over)
Yeah.

574
00:19:55,060 --> 00:19:56,160
How'd you know I needed that?

575
00:19:56,400 --> 00:19:58,200
We can read each other's minds now.

576
00:19:59,080 --> 00:20:00,240
Really?

577
00:20:00,240 --> 00:20:01,680
Xing and I can't anymore.

578
00:20:06,700 --> 00:20:08,380
(Smiles)

579
00:20:10,440 --> 00:20:11,600
So, in the future,

580
00:20:11,600 --> 00:20:13,800
wanna try more crafts?

581
00:20:13,800 --> 00:20:15,520
I'd try anything with you.

582
00:20:15,580 --> 00:20:17,720
(I'd try anything with you)

583
00:20:17,720 --> 00:20:18,920
I love doing anything with you.

584
00:20:18,940 --> 00:20:20,780
(Smiles)

585
00:20:27,360 --> 00:20:28,600
Let me tell you something.

586
00:20:30,360 --> 00:20:31,640
My cup's unbeatable. Get it?

587
00:20:31,640 --> 00:20:32,480
(Unbeatable)

588
00:20:32,480 --> 00:20:33,520
Strong and durable.

589
00:20:33,520 --> 00:20:34,520
(Strong and durable)
If one handle breaks,

590
00:20:34,520 --> 00:20:35,320
you've still got another.

591
00:20:42,240 --> 00:20:43,320
Here's a leaf for you.

592
00:20:45,020 --> 00:20:47,460
(A leaf hidden inside the cup)

593
00:20:48,680 --> 00:20:51,320
There's a story behind this leaf.

594
00:20:51,320 --> 00:20:52,280
(A leaf with a story)
What story?

595
00:20:52,280 --> 00:20:54,040
I'll tell you someday.

596
00:20:54,040 --> 00:20:54,880
Someday?

597
00:20:54,880 --> 00:20:57,400
(A story to share someday)
It's the leaf hidden inside.

598
00:21:01,380 --> 00:21:02,180
(Glances)

599
00:21:02,200 --> 00:21:03,480
Yihang, are you two done?

600
00:21:03,680 --> 00:21:04,440
Almost.

601
00:21:04,800 --> 00:21:06,880
(Gets up to look)
Is the shape finished?

602
00:21:06,880 --> 00:21:07,760
Yeah.

603
00:21:07,760 --> 00:21:10,200
All that's left now

604
00:21:10,200 --> 00:21:11,280
is maybe some paint.

605
00:21:11,590 --> 00:21:12,920
(Still needs painting)
Can I touch it?

606
00:21:13,040 --> 00:21:13,480
No.

607
00:21:13,480 --> 00:21:13,960
I can't?

608
00:21:13,960 --> 00:21:15,200
It'll lose its shape, right?

609
00:21:15,200 --> 00:21:15,800
Yeah.

610
00:21:15,800 --> 00:21:16,460
(Not fired yet)

611
00:21:16,640 --> 00:21:18,240
What's this Y for?

612
00:21:18,360 --> 00:21:19,160
Her name.

613
00:21:19,280 --> 00:21:20,680
Both her first and last names

614
00:21:20,680 --> 00:21:21,760
have that letter, right?

615
00:21:23,040 --> 00:21:24,320
Which one do you like better?

616
00:21:24,560 --> 00:21:25,560
To be fair,

617
00:21:25,760 --> 00:21:27,680
at first glance, Yihang's...

618
00:21:27,700 --> 00:21:28,400
(Pauses)

619
00:21:28,400 --> 00:21:29,280
Looks a little better?

620
00:21:30,800 --> 00:21:31,840
No.

621
00:21:31,840 --> 00:21:34,360
But...

622
00:21:34,360 --> 00:21:36,200
But it grows on you.

623
00:21:36,640 --> 00:21:38,200
You can tell Yihang put thought into it.

624
00:21:38,800 --> 00:21:40,340
(Thoughtful design)
It's got two Ys.

625
00:21:41,520 --> 00:21:43,040
Come on. You judge Si's.

626
00:21:43,360 --> 00:21:45,000
I think both look great.

627
00:21:45,360 --> 00:21:46,640
But if I had to choose,

628
00:21:46,640 --> 00:21:49,600
I'd vote for this creative cup.

629
00:21:49,600 --> 00:21:50,800
Because it's so ugly?

630
00:21:51,360 --> 00:21:52,400
Because it's so weird?

631
00:21:52,760 --> 00:21:54,040
Because it's creative.

632
00:21:54,040 --> 00:21:54,920
It's one of a kind.

633
00:21:54,920 --> 00:21:56,760
You know, the greatest works of art

634
00:21:58,400 --> 00:21:59,720
(Si's POV)
are often misunderstood.

635
00:22:00,380 --> 00:22:01,320
(Smooth talker)

636
00:22:01,320 --> 00:22:02,320
In the future,

637
00:22:02,320 --> 00:22:02,960
a hundred years from now,

638
00:22:02,960 --> 00:22:04,340
this'll be a masterpiece.

639
00:22:04,340 --> 00:22:04,980
(Thinking ahead)

640
00:22:05,760 --> 00:22:06,600
Nobody will understand

641
00:22:06,600 --> 00:22:07,560
why it has two handles.

642
00:22:07,840 --> 00:22:08,360
Exactly.

643
00:22:08,840 --> 00:22:10,200
We gotta paint them first.

644
00:22:10,200 --> 00:22:11,160
You haven't painted them?

645
00:22:11,440 --> 00:22:12,140
Okay.

646
00:22:12,140 --> 00:22:13,860
(Final painting)

647
00:22:16,260 --> 00:22:17,460
(Smiles)

648
00:22:17,460 --> 00:22:18,240
It's just so weird.

649
00:22:18,240 --> 00:22:19,240
Know what I mean?

650
00:22:20,400 --> 00:22:21,800
I think it's pretty good.

651
00:22:21,820 --> 00:22:23,740
(Encouraging him)

652
00:22:28,080 --> 00:22:29,320
We can sit here.

653
00:22:29,320 --> 00:22:30,440
I'll sit inside then.

654
00:22:30,440 --> 00:22:31,240
Sure.

655
00:22:32,680 --> 00:22:34,480
Where do you guys wanna go next?

656
00:22:35,080 --> 00:22:36,210
Yihang, let's catch some fish.

657
00:22:36,210 --> 00:22:36,720
(Invites him fishing)

658
00:22:36,720 --> 00:22:37,520
Sure.

659
00:22:38,160 --> 00:22:38,840
I'm ready.

660
00:22:39,520 --> 00:22:40,000
All done?

661
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:40,760
Let's go then.

662
00:22:41,120 --> 00:22:41,760
Okay.

663
00:22:42,200 --> 00:22:42,760
Let's go.

664
00:22:43,280 --> 00:22:44,400
Let's catch some fish!

665
00:22:45,040 --> 00:22:45,840
Little fishies!

666
00:22:46,470 --> 00:22:47,320
Watch your head.

667
00:22:47,430 --> 00:22:48,560
Careful!

668
00:22:48,560 --> 00:22:49,940
Don't hurt the tree!

669
00:22:49,940 --> 00:22:51,700
(Teasing)

670
00:22:52,960 --> 00:22:55,160
We can use these nets from the shore.

671
00:22:55,160 --> 00:22:55,600
That works.

672
00:22:55,600 --> 00:22:56,200
Really?

673
00:22:56,200 --> 00:22:56,960
You can still catch them.

674
00:22:57,880 --> 00:22:59,680
How many fish to win?

675
00:22:59,680 --> 00:23:00,520
First to three wins.

676
00:23:00,520 --> 00:23:02,280
Then whoever loses today...

677
00:23:04,480 --> 00:23:06,000
has to do the dishes tonight. Deal?

678
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:06,680
(Loser does the dishes)

679
00:23:06,680 --> 00:23:07,240
Deal.

680
00:23:07,240 --> 00:23:08,440
(Agrees immediately)

681
00:23:08,440 --> 00:23:10,120
(Straight to fishing)
Xing, step back a little.

682
00:23:10,120 --> 00:23:11,440
Okay, you stay over there.

683
00:23:11,440 --> 00:23:13,240
I'll watch for them here.

684
00:23:13,240 --> 00:23:13,960
This is so hard.

685
00:23:13,960 --> 00:23:15,200
Let's just catch any that come by.

686
00:23:16,200 --> 00:23:17,760
Maybe we'll catch a few here.

687
00:23:22,040 --> 00:23:22,720
Got one!

688
00:23:23,880 --> 00:23:24,420
Got one!

689
00:23:24,420 --> 00:23:25,100
(Bohan catches his first fish)

690
00:23:25,100 --> 00:23:26,920
I'm already one point ahead.

691
00:23:26,920 --> 00:23:27,880
That was fast.

692
00:23:27,880 --> 00:23:28,920
Come on, Yihang.

693
00:23:29,680 --> 00:23:30,280
Let's change.

694
00:23:30,280 --> 00:23:31,560
Seriously, let's get changed.

695
00:23:33,200 --> 00:23:34,560
(Geared up)
Let's get in the water.

696
00:23:34,600 --> 00:23:35,160
Let's go.

697
00:23:37,540 --> 00:23:39,340
(Still getting dressed)

698
00:23:39,360 --> 00:23:40,760
How'd you do up the back?

699
00:23:44,680 --> 00:23:45,480
Here.

700
00:23:46,440 --> 00:23:47,230
Like this?

701
00:23:47,240 --> 00:23:48,200
(Helps out)
Yeah.

702
00:23:48,200 --> 00:23:49,440
Yeah, open this up.

703
00:23:49,440 --> 00:23:50,240
Like this?

704
00:23:50,240 --> 00:23:50,960
Yeah.

705
00:23:50,960 --> 00:23:52,400
Keep pulling it down. Yeah.

706
00:23:52,840 --> 00:23:54,600
They're helping each other get dressed.

707
00:23:54,600 --> 00:23:56,020
(Glances)

708
00:23:57,240 --> 00:23:59,440
Ever feel like you
can predict the future?

709
00:23:59,440 --> 00:24:00,720
Really? Like what?

710
00:24:00,960 --> 00:24:01,680
Back at the Signal House,

711
00:24:01,680 --> 00:24:03,160
I think I imagined this moment.

712
00:24:03,160 --> 00:24:04,600
Them helping each other get dressed.

713
00:24:04,600 --> 00:24:05,360
(Imagined this exact scene)

714
00:24:05,360 --> 00:24:06,400
Them together?

715
00:24:07,880 --> 00:24:09,800
Come on. Should we just get in?

716
00:24:09,800 --> 00:24:10,880
Yeah, let's go.

717
00:24:11,400 --> 00:24:12,320
Take it slow.

718
00:24:18,340 --> 00:24:19,460
(Yihang catches his first fish)

719
00:24:19,480 --> 00:24:20,440
Nice!

720
00:24:20,880 --> 00:24:21,720
He got one.

721
00:24:22,180 --> 00:24:24,020
(Rushing it to the bucket)

722
00:24:25,520 --> 00:24:26,920
It's one to one now.

723
00:24:27,440 --> 00:24:29,040
There! By your feet!

724
00:24:29,800 --> 00:24:30,400
See it?

725
00:24:30,920 --> 00:24:31,720
Slowly.

726
00:24:31,720 --> 00:24:33,320
Don't scare it away.

727
00:24:33,320 --> 00:24:34,200
Right, don't scare it.

728
00:24:34,200 --> 00:24:34,600
Easy.

729
00:24:38,260 --> 00:24:39,980
(Yihang catches his second fish)

730
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:41,440
Yihang's got two!

731
00:24:41,440 --> 00:24:42,160
Already?

732
00:24:42,880 --> 00:24:44,640
You're putting me
under pressure, Yihang!

733
00:24:51,620 --> 00:24:53,060
(Yihang catches his third fish)

734
00:24:53,080 --> 00:24:54,080
You win!

735
00:24:56,560 --> 00:24:57,920
Yihang's a fishing pro!

736
00:24:58,320 --> 00:24:59,580
(Fishing pro)
A fishing pro!

737
00:24:59,600 --> 00:25:00,320
A bet's a bet.

738
00:25:00,320 --> 00:25:01,880
Tonight,

739
00:25:01,880 --> 00:25:02,760
I'm doing the dishes.

740
00:25:03,420 --> 00:25:05,180
(Fishing pro)

741
00:25:07,260 --> 00:25:08,940
(Beijing Airport)

742
00:25:08,980 --> 00:25:10,240
(11:05AM, Yu Yang arrives in Beijing)

743
00:25:10,240 --> 00:25:12,480
I'm back in Beijing.

744
00:25:23,320 --> 00:25:25,080
Who is it?

745
00:25:25,080 --> 00:25:26,500
Ding-dong!

746
00:25:28,880 --> 00:25:29,950
I'm back!

747
00:25:33,340 --> 00:25:35,740
(Me too!)

748
00:25:36,560 --> 00:25:37,080
Sparkle.

749
00:25:41,000 --> 00:25:42,520
You're too much!

750
00:25:42,520 --> 00:25:43,920
Look what I brought you.

751
00:25:44,880 --> 00:25:46,220
(A gift for Sparkle)
What's that?

752
00:25:46,240 --> 00:25:48,920
What's this? Look,
it's licking its lips!

753
00:25:48,920 --> 00:25:50,800
It really thinks it's food!

754
00:25:50,800 --> 00:25:51,680
Alright.

755
00:25:51,680 --> 00:25:52,480
Missed me that much?

756
00:25:53,000 --> 00:25:54,520
That much?

757
00:25:56,000 --> 00:25:57,120
Careful!

758
00:25:57,480 --> 00:26:00,080
It can't handle it anymore.
It's all like this!

759
00:26:11,980 --> 00:26:13,580
(Laughs)

760
00:26:13,580 --> 00:26:14,640
Should we let it loose first?

761
00:26:14,640 --> 00:26:16,160
I'll wipe its paws first.

762
00:26:16,160 --> 00:26:16,520
Yeah.

763
00:26:19,240 --> 00:26:21,480
It always looks so confused
when I wipe its paws.

764
00:26:21,500 --> 00:26:22,560
(Totally confused)

765
00:26:22,560 --> 00:26:23,280
What's wrong?

766
00:26:23,280 --> 00:26:24,880
It's like, what's going on?

767
00:26:24,880 --> 00:26:26,440
(Wipes its paws)
You're getting spoiled now too.

768
00:26:29,000 --> 00:26:30,320
It'll shake it right off.

769
00:26:35,840 --> 00:26:36,720
You've already seen it.

770
00:26:36,720 --> 00:26:37,400
So here you go.

771
00:26:37,400 --> 00:26:37,960
What?

772
00:26:37,960 --> 00:26:38,400
Flowers.

773
00:26:39,080 --> 00:26:41,640
Thank you.

774
00:26:42,440 --> 00:26:44,400
You can just pull it out like this.

775
00:26:44,400 --> 00:26:45,400
(To my baby,
happy one-month anniversary!)

776
00:26:45,400 --> 00:26:46,360
(May we grow happier every day!)
It's been a month.

777
00:26:46,360 --> 00:26:48,160
(YuLiang Never Fades, stronger together!)
One month. This is for you.

778
00:26:51,480 --> 00:26:53,840
A gift? Thank you!

779
00:26:57,720 --> 00:26:58,680
Looks good.

780
00:26:58,680 --> 00:27:00,080
Remember how you said the other day

781
00:27:00,080 --> 00:27:02,080
you didn't have a cap like this?

782
00:27:02,080 --> 00:27:02,840
Yeah, I've never had one.

783
00:27:02,840 --> 00:27:04,760
Then I happened to find this one.

784
00:27:04,760 --> 00:27:05,960
I thought it'd suit you.

785
00:27:05,960 --> 00:27:07,560
It's got some nice little details,

786
00:27:07,560 --> 00:27:09,240
but it's not too flashy.

787
00:27:09,940 --> 00:27:10,960
(Smiles)

788
00:27:10,960 --> 00:27:11,800
I'm happy.

789
00:27:17,120 --> 00:27:17,800
Looks good.

790
00:27:18,440 --> 00:27:21,160
Yesterday was our...

791
00:27:21,800 --> 00:27:22,280
One-month anniversary.

792
00:27:22,280 --> 00:27:24,080
Our one-month anniversary,
but I wasn't here.

793
00:27:25,080 --> 00:27:28,560
So I thought today we could

794
00:27:28,560 --> 00:27:30,680
- celebrate it together.
- Okay, so we're

795
00:27:30,680 --> 00:27:32,200
one day past our anniversary.

796
00:27:32,200 --> 00:27:33,160
Exactly.

797
00:27:33,160 --> 00:27:34,080
As for what we're doing,

798
00:27:34,080 --> 00:27:35,040
leave it to me.

799
00:27:35,040 --> 00:27:36,400
- I've got it all planned.
- Okay.

800
00:27:37,040 --> 00:27:38,480
Shall we go?

801
00:27:38,480 --> 00:27:39,080
Yeah.

802
00:27:39,080 --> 00:27:39,480
Let's go.

803
00:27:39,820 --> 00:27:41,240
(Fang's POV)

804
00:27:41,240 --> 00:27:42,240
Where are we going?

805
00:27:42,240 --> 00:27:46,320
We're going to...

806
00:27:46,320 --> 00:27:47,400
somewhere mysterious.

807
00:27:47,400 --> 00:27:48,960
See? You still won't tell me!

808
00:27:48,960 --> 00:27:51,000
I've tried everything
to get it out of you!

809
00:27:57,800 --> 00:27:59,040
All in one bite.

810
00:28:06,840 --> 00:28:08,160
We can get out now.

811
00:28:10,760 --> 00:28:12,080
After you.

812
00:28:12,980 --> 00:28:15,560
(Handmade jewelry shop)

813
00:28:15,560 --> 00:28:19,280
I found out that this place lets you

814
00:28:19,280 --> 00:28:22,040
make your own rings.

815
00:28:22,040 --> 00:28:23,440
Since it's

816
00:28:24,680 --> 00:28:25,720
our anniversary,

817
00:28:25,720 --> 00:28:26,960
we could make

818
00:28:26,960 --> 00:28:29,720
(Making anniversary rings)
something special to remember it by.

819
00:28:30,240 --> 00:28:32,120
I didn't see this coming at all.

820
00:28:32,120 --> 00:28:32,600
Not at all.

821
00:28:32,600 --> 00:28:33,600
I kept guessing...

822
00:28:33,600 --> 00:28:34,280
But you never got it.

823
00:28:34,280 --> 00:28:34,880
Nope.

824
00:28:36,080 --> 00:28:37,000
This one...

825
00:28:37,260 --> 00:28:38,560
This wider one looks pretty nice.

826
00:28:38,560 --> 00:28:39,360
Or this one looks good too.

827
00:28:39,800 --> 00:28:40,320
Yeah.

828
00:28:40,320 --> 00:28:42,320
It's got a center stone.

829
00:28:42,320 --> 00:28:43,060
"Main course"?

830
00:28:43,060 --> 00:28:44,160
(Laughs)

831
00:28:44,160 --> 00:28:44,880
You're hungry.

832
00:28:46,040 --> 00:28:46,840
What do you think?

833
00:28:46,840 --> 00:28:47,200
Looks good.

834
00:28:47,200 --> 00:28:48,080
Let's go with this one.

835
00:28:50,400 --> 00:28:52,120
My hands are shaking!

836
00:28:52,420 --> 00:28:52,940
(Glances)

837
00:28:55,000 --> 00:28:55,560
Let me see.

838
00:28:55,560 --> 00:28:56,600
Look at my heart.

839
00:28:56,600 --> 00:28:57,580
(Leans closer)

840
00:28:57,640 --> 00:28:58,320
A little Y

841
00:28:58,320 --> 00:28:59,120
and a big Y.

842
00:28:59,120 --> 00:29:00,120
So pretty.

843
00:29:00,400 --> 00:29:01,160
Careful.

844
00:29:01,400 --> 00:29:02,720
Press the one at the back.

845
00:29:05,360 --> 00:29:06,440
Sixteen point five.

846
00:29:06,760 --> 00:29:07,560
Okay.

847
00:29:08,640 --> 00:29:10,040
Watch your hands.

848
00:29:10,040 --> 00:29:11,160
Okay, you too.

849
00:29:14,560 --> 00:29:15,800
That should do it.

850
00:29:16,680 --> 00:29:17,120
Z.

851
00:29:17,120 --> 00:29:17,760
Perfect fit.

852
00:29:18,160 --> 00:29:19,680
I remember your ring size

853
00:29:19,680 --> 00:29:20,480
matches my pinky.

854
00:29:24,440 --> 00:29:25,360
I did my research.

855
00:29:27,160 --> 00:29:28,480
I really did.

856
00:29:28,480 --> 00:29:30,120
The one you wore
at the Signal House was that size.

857
00:29:30,680 --> 00:29:31,480
Beautiful!

858
00:29:31,480 --> 00:29:32,680
I'll get someone

859
00:29:32,680 --> 00:29:33,560
to set the stones for you.

860
00:29:33,560 --> 00:29:34,760
Okay, thank you.

861
00:29:34,760 --> 00:29:35,120
Okay.

862
00:29:35,140 --> 00:29:37,780
(The shop handles the gemstone setting)

863
00:29:39,600 --> 00:29:41,040
Thank you!

864
00:29:41,440 --> 00:29:43,000
Look at that! So nice!

865
00:29:43,320 --> 00:29:44,320
So pretty!

866
00:29:44,800 --> 00:29:45,720
Let's take a picture.

867
00:29:45,720 --> 00:29:46,480
Let's do it.

868
00:29:49,360 --> 00:29:50,600
The lettering's so pretty!

869
00:29:50,600 --> 00:29:51,480
Wanna put it on?

870
00:30:03,040 --> 00:30:03,840
Success!

871
00:30:05,440 --> 00:30:06,240
Perfect!

872
00:30:06,680 --> 00:30:07,440
Fits perfectly.

873
00:30:07,440 --> 00:30:08,360
Yeah, your turn.

874
00:30:12,240 --> 00:30:13,280
Perfect fit.

875
00:30:17,040 --> 00:30:18,000
Looks great.

876
00:30:21,320 --> 00:30:22,160
So pretty.

877
00:30:22,760 --> 00:30:24,800
Happy anniversary!

878
00:30:30,760 --> 00:30:32,040
Let's eat!

879
00:30:32,040 --> 00:30:33,240
Let's eat! What are we having?

880
00:30:33,240 --> 00:30:34,520
I've got it covered.

881
00:30:37,520 --> 00:30:39,600
We're home!

882
00:30:40,860 --> 00:30:41,520
(Yu Yang's home)

883
00:30:41,520 --> 00:30:42,760
Let's cook first.

884
00:30:42,760 --> 00:30:43,360
Okay.

885
00:30:43,360 --> 00:30:44,000
I'm hungry!

886
00:30:44,000 --> 00:30:45,320
Let's eat!

887
00:30:45,320 --> 00:30:47,160
Let's get some rice cooking first.

888
00:30:47,160 --> 00:30:47,880
I'll rinse it.

889
00:30:47,900 --> 00:30:48,540
(Working together)

890
00:30:48,540 --> 00:30:51,640
You do that. I'll get the ingredients.

891
00:30:53,640 --> 00:30:55,280
The scallion, ginger, and garlic trio.

892
00:30:56,320 --> 00:30:57,320
So what's for dinner?

893
00:30:57,500 --> 00:30:58,960
Your favorite mapo tofu.

894
00:31:00,980 --> 00:31:02,740
(Ingredients prepared in advance)
It's gonna take a while.

895
00:31:14,110 --> 00:31:15,800
It's so hot. I'm taking my jacket off.

896
00:31:16,080 --> 00:31:16,940
Can you help me...

897
00:31:16,940 --> 00:31:18,400
Peel some garlic? How many cloves?

898
00:31:18,400 --> 00:31:19,200
Four or five.

899
00:31:19,200 --> 00:31:20,000
Four or five?

900
00:31:25,200 --> 00:31:26,040
Let's blanch the ribs.

901
00:31:31,640 --> 00:31:32,720
Already?

902
00:31:33,100 --> 00:31:35,280
I've forgotten the steps.

903
00:31:35,280 --> 00:31:35,900
Really?

904
00:31:37,210 --> 00:31:38,880
I even got a cheat sheet from my mom.

905
00:31:39,960 --> 00:31:41,320
I think she wrote it for me.

906
00:31:41,320 --> 00:31:42,360
I can't even remember.

907
00:31:42,650 --> 00:31:44,520
I followed...

908
00:31:45,450 --> 00:31:46,750
your mom's recipe exactly.

909
00:31:46,750 --> 00:31:47,600
(Following Fang's mom's recipe)
Really?

910
00:31:47,600 --> 00:31:48,280
Yeah.

911
00:31:48,280 --> 00:31:50,190
You followed my mom's recipe?

912
00:31:50,190 --> 00:31:50,840
Yeah.

913
00:31:53,400 --> 00:31:54,680
It already smells amazing.

914
00:31:54,680 --> 00:31:56,260
(Happy)

915
00:31:56,600 --> 00:31:57,840
Or we could switch things up.

916
00:31:57,840 --> 00:31:59,520
How about stir-fried ribs instead?

917
00:32:00,240 --> 00:32:01,440
(Switching to stir-fried ribs?)
Stir-fried ribs?

918
00:32:01,440 --> 00:32:02,580
(Requests sweet and sour ribs)
Sweet and sour ribs!

919
00:32:02,600 --> 00:32:03,400
Sure!

920
00:32:03,760 --> 00:32:04,280
Let's do it!

921
00:32:04,640 --> 00:32:05,520
Two spoonfuls of light soy sauce.

922
00:32:05,520 --> 00:32:06,320
Okay.

923
00:32:08,360 --> 00:32:09,240
Now just let it cook.

924
00:32:09,490 --> 00:32:10,880
(Waiting for it to cook)
Both pans at once.

925
00:32:10,880 --> 00:32:11,920
Mapo tofu!

926
00:32:11,920 --> 00:32:13,520
(Making extra-meaty mapo tofu)
It's tofu with ground pork.

927
00:32:15,840 --> 00:32:16,260
I'll do it.

928
00:32:16,260 --> 00:32:16,960
(Takes over)

929
00:32:16,960 --> 00:32:17,880
It's okay.

930
00:32:20,720 --> 00:32:22,680
Okay, give it a stir.

931
00:32:22,960 --> 00:32:23,560
Stir it.

932
00:32:31,600 --> 00:32:33,400
The secret sauce.

933
00:32:37,160 --> 00:32:38,520
Time to add the tofu!

934
00:32:39,000 --> 00:32:39,800
Let's go!

935
00:32:40,160 --> 00:32:40,810
Give it to me.

936
00:32:40,980 --> 00:32:42,220
(Takes the spatula)

937
00:32:50,920 --> 00:32:52,000
Smells amazing!

938
00:32:52,680 --> 00:32:55,320
A man who can cook is so attractive.

939
00:32:55,340 --> 00:32:56,380
(An attractive man who can cook)

940
00:32:56,420 --> 00:32:57,580
(Mapo tofu is ready)

941
00:32:58,800 --> 00:32:59,760
Over here?

942
00:33:00,120 --> 00:33:00,640
Up to you.

943
00:33:00,640 --> 00:33:03,040
If you wanna watch TV,
we can eat at the coffee table.

944
00:33:03,960 --> 00:33:06,280
Shall we sit on the couch then?

945
00:33:07,160 --> 00:33:07,840
Sure.

946
00:33:07,840 --> 00:33:09,000
I'll clear this up.

947
00:33:09,020 --> 00:33:10,260
(Clearing the coffee table)

948
00:33:14,200 --> 00:33:15,760
The ribs are almost ready!

949
00:33:15,760 --> 00:33:17,560
The ribs are what? Ready?

950
00:33:19,380 --> 00:33:21,340
(Ground pork with long beans, mapo tofu)

951
00:33:22,160 --> 00:33:23,450
Impressive!

952
00:33:24,120 --> 00:33:24,960
This smells great.

953
00:33:26,560 --> 00:33:27,720
Seriously!

954
00:33:31,960 --> 00:33:32,800
Amazing!

955
00:33:35,220 --> 00:33:36,160
(A feast for dinner)

956
00:33:36,160 --> 00:33:38,160
Five dishes for two people.

957
00:33:38,160 --> 00:33:39,400
It's like New Year's.

958
00:33:39,400 --> 00:33:40,000
Let's celebrate.

959
00:33:40,600 --> 00:33:42,040
Cheers!

960
00:33:46,260 --> 00:33:47,360
What do you think?

961
00:33:47,360 --> 00:33:49,360
Let me try this mapo tofu.

962
00:33:49,840 --> 00:33:52,600
Let me have a taste of this tofu!

963
00:33:52,740 --> 00:33:53,820
(The first bite goes
to the hardworking chef)

964
00:33:56,240 --> 00:33:57,040
Delicious!

965
00:33:58,280 --> 00:33:59,120
So good!

966
00:33:59,760 --> 00:34:00,320
Delicious!

967
00:34:04,840 --> 00:34:06,280
This is so good!

968
00:34:06,680 --> 00:34:07,600
Have a bite.

969
00:34:07,600 --> 00:34:08,600
Thanks.

970
00:34:12,800 --> 00:34:14,560
It really feels better to be home.

971
00:34:16,320 --> 00:34:17,520
It feels like home.

972
00:34:17,520 --> 00:34:19,000
My family makes these dishes too.

973
00:34:20,480 --> 00:34:22,120
I really love eating at home.

974
00:34:22,920 --> 00:34:24,230
You know, even after working

975
00:34:25,040 --> 00:34:26,210
for all these years,

976
00:34:26,560 --> 00:34:27,400
I'd usually

977
00:34:27,770 --> 00:34:29,720
go home once a week
when I wasn't too busy

978
00:34:30,430 --> 00:34:31,600
just to have a meal.

979
00:34:32,680 --> 00:34:34,440
I wouldn't even stay the night.

980
00:34:35,120 --> 00:34:36,400
I'd just go home to eat.

981
00:34:36,840 --> 00:34:38,400
Because eating at home

982
00:34:38,400 --> 00:34:40,600
(Home-cooked meals mean a lot)
means a lot to me.

983
00:34:42,720 --> 00:34:45,320
I'm away from home so much,

984
00:34:45,320 --> 00:34:47,280
always traveling for work

985
00:34:47,280 --> 00:34:47,800
and everything.

986
00:34:48,120 --> 00:34:48,480
Yeah.

987
00:34:48,960 --> 00:34:50,200
When I was at my busiest,

988
00:34:50,200 --> 00:34:52,160
I probably barely had

989
00:34:52,160 --> 00:34:55,160
a few meals at home all year.

990
00:34:56,600 --> 00:34:58,890
So, yeah.

991
00:35:01,960 --> 00:35:03,200
I feel like being home

992
00:35:03,680 --> 00:35:04,960
and getting

993
00:35:05,960 --> 00:35:06,840
to cook for you

994
00:35:06,840 --> 00:35:08,440
makes me really happy.

995
00:35:11,040 --> 00:35:11,800
Thanks for all your hard work.

996
00:35:11,800 --> 00:35:13,080
Cooking for you recharges me too.

997
00:35:13,100 --> 00:35:15,220
(Massages his shoulders)

998
00:35:18,880 --> 00:35:20,720
It's not like we're
skipping a special celebration.

999
00:35:20,720 --> 00:35:22,920
Exactly! This
is our special celebration.

1000
00:35:22,920 --> 00:35:23,760
Yeah.

1001
00:35:23,760 --> 00:35:26,520
In our month together,

1002
00:35:26,520 --> 00:35:29,280
this is our first proper time
cooking together.

1003
00:35:29,800 --> 00:35:33,000
So it's really special.

1004
00:35:33,000 --> 00:35:34,120
Very special.

1005
00:35:34,760 --> 00:35:36,400
I remember
when my sister-in-law was pregnant,

1006
00:35:36,400 --> 00:35:38,320
my brother cooked at home every day.

1007
00:35:41,080 --> 00:35:41,960
I was thinking when I get a boyfriend,

1008
00:35:41,960 --> 00:35:43,080
he has to know how to cook!

1009
00:35:43,080 --> 00:35:44,040
Know how to cook?

1010
00:35:44,040 --> 00:35:44,920
Yeah.

1011
00:35:46,040 --> 00:35:50,480
Next time, I'll really prepare

1012
00:35:50,480 --> 00:35:52,040
and let you try my cooking.

1013
00:35:52,040 --> 00:35:53,680
But I wanna do it all

1014
00:35:53,960 --> 00:35:55,560
by myself.

1015
00:35:55,560 --> 00:35:57,080
I'll stand by with a fire extinguisher!

1016
00:35:59,660 --> 00:36:01,120
Already teasing me?

1017
00:36:01,240 --> 00:36:02,600
Then you can cook from now on,

1018
00:36:02,600 --> 00:36:03,240
and I'll do the dishes.

1019
00:36:03,240 --> 00:36:04,400
(Fair division of chores)
Deal.

1020
00:36:04,440 --> 00:36:06,280
The dishwashing crew
still loves doing dishes.

1021
00:36:06,300 --> 00:36:07,680
(The house's dishwashing crew)

1022
00:36:07,680 --> 00:36:08,520
Speaking of which,

1023
00:36:08,520 --> 00:36:09,520
do you think Yiheng and Kaiyi

1024
00:36:09,520 --> 00:36:11,440
fight over who gets to...

1025
00:36:11,960 --> 00:36:12,840
Do the dishes every day?

1026
00:36:12,840 --> 00:36:13,720
Fight over doing dishes?

1027
00:36:13,720 --> 00:36:14,360
They'd be fighting!

1028
00:36:14,360 --> 00:36:15,800
I'll do it!

1029
00:36:15,800 --> 00:36:16,840
No, you will!

1030
00:36:17,600 --> 00:36:19,960
Didn't they get together
over washing dishes?

1031
00:36:21,800 --> 00:36:22,520
But seriously,

1032
00:36:22,520 --> 00:36:23,480
I think couples

1033
00:36:23,480 --> 00:36:25,120
doing chores together,

1034
00:36:25,120 --> 00:36:26,600
whether it's cooking

1035
00:36:26,600 --> 00:36:28,400
or washing dishes,

1036
00:36:28,880 --> 00:36:30,320
can be really sweet.

1037
00:36:31,640 --> 00:36:32,880
Same here.

1038
00:36:32,880 --> 00:36:33,960
Having you by my side

1039
00:36:33,960 --> 00:36:36,480
while I cook feels so cozy.

1040
00:36:40,020 --> 00:36:41,180
(Deep in thought)

1041
00:36:43,520 --> 00:36:44,760
You haven't seen that room yet.

1042
00:36:46,480 --> 00:36:47,480
Come on, I'll show you.

1043
00:36:47,500 --> 00:36:48,800
(Invites her to see his workspace)

1044
00:36:48,800 --> 00:36:49,720
A little tour!

1045
00:36:49,720 --> 00:36:50,920
A proper tour of my room.

1046
00:36:50,920 --> 00:36:51,720
Okay!

1047
00:36:52,640 --> 00:36:53,440
Have a look.

1048
00:36:55,680 --> 00:36:56,600
This room...

1049
00:36:57,350 --> 00:36:58,590
Liang Renfang!

1050
00:36:59,500 --> 00:37:00,760
(Liang Renfang)

1051
00:37:00,760 --> 00:37:01,920
Why am I

1052
00:37:01,920 --> 00:37:03,600
on this rabbit?

1053
00:37:04,880 --> 00:37:07,080
The first thing I did
when I got back was...

1054
00:37:07,080 --> 00:37:08,600
Pin this on the rabbit.

1055
00:37:08,600 --> 00:37:08,920
Yeah.

1056
00:37:08,920 --> 00:37:10,280
(Liang Renfang)

1057
00:37:10,280 --> 00:37:12,320
Well, thanks a lot!

1058
00:37:12,320 --> 00:37:13,280
Seriously!

1059
00:37:15,360 --> 00:37:16,280
What's this?

1060
00:37:16,300 --> 00:37:17,260
(Yu Yang's workstation)

1061
00:37:17,260 --> 00:37:18,320
It's a synthesizer.

1062
00:37:19,440 --> 00:37:21,720
You play around with this at home?

1063
00:37:21,720 --> 00:37:22,760
Yeah.

1064
00:37:22,820 --> 00:37:24,380
(Looks around)

1065
00:37:27,460 --> 00:37:28,740
(Opens it)

1066
00:37:29,000 --> 00:37:29,440
Wait!

1067
00:37:36,460 --> 00:37:38,700
(Diary of Fang)

1068
00:37:40,160 --> 00:37:41,080
What's this?

1069
00:37:41,080 --> 00:37:43,840
You brought me in here on purpose!

1070
00:37:46,320 --> 00:37:48,040
What if I hadn't found it?

1071
00:37:48,040 --> 00:37:49,000
If you hadn't...

1072
00:37:49,000 --> 00:37:50,320
Well, you found it!

1073
00:37:52,720 --> 00:37:53,880
When did you draw these?

1074
00:37:55,360 --> 00:37:56,800
Before I went to Guangzhou.

1075
00:37:56,800 --> 00:37:57,920
That's when you started.

1076
00:38:02,640 --> 00:38:03,440
Let me see.

1077
00:38:03,440 --> 00:38:04,440
Go ahead.

1078
00:38:07,710 --> 00:38:09,840
The day we shook hands...

1079
00:38:09,840 --> 00:38:11,320
Hello, boyfriend.

1080
00:38:12,400 --> 00:38:13,200
Hello,

1081
00:38:14,080 --> 00:38:14,920
boyfriend!

1082
00:38:15,920 --> 00:38:17,000
Hello, girlfriend!

1083
00:38:20,660 --> 00:38:22,620
(June 12, 2026.
You officially became my girlfriend.)

1084
00:38:22,620 --> 00:38:24,340
(I wanted to capture our special moments
this month through drawings.)

1085
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:31,080
So detailed.

1086
00:38:32,920 --> 00:38:34,560
I'm holding the bag here,

1087
00:38:34,560 --> 00:38:36,240
and you're picking up poop!

1088
00:38:48,340 --> 00:38:51,100
(I'm so happy.)

1089
00:38:51,120 --> 00:38:52,560
This is so cute!

1090
00:38:56,700 --> 00:39:00,220
(I'm so happy.)

1091
00:39:01,140 --> 00:39:02,700
(We'll always be together.)

1092
00:39:04,320 --> 00:39:06,280
I changed the title a little too.

1093
00:39:07,280 --> 00:39:08,520
Now it's "Our diary".

1094
00:39:09,180 --> 00:39:10,680
It used to be "Observation diary".

1095
00:39:10,680 --> 00:39:11,720
Yeah.

1096
00:39:11,720 --> 00:39:13,640
An upgrade.

1097
00:39:13,640 --> 00:39:15,320
From observing to being together.

1098
00:39:17,320 --> 00:39:19,480
Well, I'm looking forward
to your next...

1099
00:39:19,480 --> 00:39:20,280
My next masterpiece!

1100
00:39:20,280 --> 00:39:21,080
The next one!

1101
00:39:23,640 --> 00:39:24,800
You can add a few strokes.

1102
00:39:26,600 --> 00:39:28,320
I'll just finish this heart.

1103
00:39:28,320 --> 00:39:29,760
Just the heart?

1104
00:39:32,960 --> 00:39:33,680
Done!

1105
00:39:38,480 --> 00:39:41,200
Wow. You made it look so 3D.

1106
00:39:42,160 --> 00:39:43,040
Beautiful!

1107
00:39:43,660 --> 00:39:49,860
(Liang Renfang)

1108
00:39:49,860 --> 00:39:52,780
(Diary of Fang)

1109
00:39:56,880 --> 00:39:57,800
Okay, let's get out.

1110
00:39:59,880 --> 00:40:01,240
There are kittens!

1111
00:40:03,040 --> 00:40:03,840
Thanks.

1112
00:40:07,320 --> 00:40:08,360
This is so pretty.

1113
00:40:08,640 --> 00:40:09,440
Yeah.

1114
00:40:11,600 --> 00:40:12,400
Here.

1115
00:40:13,260 --> 00:40:16,420
(Sets up the canvas)

1116
00:40:17,040 --> 00:40:17,760
Here you go.

1117
00:40:20,320 --> 00:40:22,080
I actually couldn't draw at all before.

1118
00:40:22,080 --> 00:40:22,760
I still can't.

1119
00:40:23,280 --> 00:40:25,360
At first, I could only draw
stick figures.

1120
00:40:25,360 --> 00:40:27,520
I think these
are pretty much stick figures.

1121
00:40:27,520 --> 00:40:28,640
Just with color.

1122
00:40:28,960 --> 00:40:30,840
I think your idea of stick figures

1123
00:40:30,840 --> 00:40:32,280
is different from mine.

1124
00:40:33,560 --> 00:40:34,360
Not really.

1125
00:40:34,360 --> 00:40:35,360
Back at the house,

1126
00:40:35,360 --> 00:40:36,480
weren't you always

1127
00:40:36,480 --> 00:40:38,360
helping me fill in the colors?

1128
00:40:39,360 --> 00:40:40,560
We can color the clothes.

1129
00:40:40,560 --> 00:40:41,600
I can do that.

1130
00:40:41,600 --> 00:40:42,280
(Painting together)
Sure.

1131
00:40:43,520 --> 00:40:44,320
So even.

1132
00:40:45,400 --> 00:40:46,720
Not bad.

1133
00:40:46,720 --> 00:40:47,080
Nice!

1134
00:40:47,080 --> 00:40:48,360
You do the outlines.

1135
00:40:48,360 --> 00:40:49,360
I'll color them in.

1136
00:40:50,640 --> 00:40:53,160
I'm almost getting the hang of drawing.

1137
00:40:55,100 --> 00:40:56,640
(Smiles shyly)

1138
00:40:56,640 --> 00:40:58,480
I actually think we can

1139
00:40:58,480 --> 00:41:00,240
just fill in the colors and be done.

1140
00:41:00,240 --> 00:41:00,640
Okay.

1141
00:41:00,640 --> 00:41:01,320
Whatever you say.

1142
00:41:01,320 --> 00:41:02,120
I'll start coloring then.

1143
00:41:02,400 --> 00:41:04,320
I'll start with the easiest part.

1144
00:41:05,080 --> 00:41:05,920
Which is...

1145
00:41:06,540 --> 00:41:09,440
I'll pick a hair color for you first.

1146
00:41:10,680 --> 00:41:12,040
Our paintings might end up

1147
00:41:12,040 --> 00:41:13,200
with the exact same colors.

1148
00:41:15,640 --> 00:41:17,880
Our hair's the same color now.

1149
00:41:17,880 --> 00:41:19,640
(Matching hair and outfit colors)
So are our clothes.

1150
00:41:19,640 --> 00:41:22,160
But I can't find dark brown.

1151
00:41:22,160 --> 00:41:24,280
I'd be okay with purple hair too.

1152
00:41:25,240 --> 00:41:26,540
(Glances)
What color would you dye yours?

1153
00:41:26,540 --> 00:41:27,180
(Glances again)

1154
00:41:27,200 --> 00:41:29,080
I want whatever color you want.

1155
00:41:31,000 --> 00:41:33,120
I want whatever color you want.

1156
00:41:33,120 --> 00:41:34,140
(What you want is what I want)

1157
00:41:49,660 --> 00:41:51,780
(Lost in painting)

1158
00:41:52,400 --> 00:41:53,320
Keep painting.

1159
00:41:53,320 --> 00:41:54,600
I'm gonna grab something outside.

1160
00:41:55,920 --> 00:41:56,720
Okay.

1161
00:42:11,580 --> 00:42:14,700
(Bags and bags)

1162
00:42:18,020 --> 00:42:19,820
(Hidden in the corner)

1163
00:42:24,320 --> 00:42:25,320
You're back.

1164
00:42:25,320 --> 00:42:25,920
Yep.

1165
00:42:32,280 --> 00:42:33,960
Yours looks so good.

1166
00:42:35,520 --> 00:42:36,960
Are those ocean waves?

1167
00:42:36,960 --> 00:42:38,120
Stop copying me!

1168
00:42:38,120 --> 00:42:39,960
You think I can even copy that?

1169
00:42:42,160 --> 00:42:43,320
Seriously!

1170
00:42:45,640 --> 00:42:48,400
I feel like it'll look good
no matter how we paint it.

1171
00:42:48,400 --> 00:42:49,200
Yeah.

1172
00:42:53,440 --> 00:42:54,680
I'm gonna use the bathroom.

1173
00:42:54,680 --> 00:42:55,600
(Gets up again)
Go ahead.

1174
00:42:55,600 --> 00:42:56,880
Take your time painting.

1175
00:43:04,060 --> 00:43:06,580
(Keeps painting)

1176
00:43:12,040 --> 00:43:12,840
You're back!

1177
00:43:12,840 --> 00:43:13,560
I'm back.

1178
00:43:13,560 --> 00:43:15,080
Feeling any better?

1179
00:43:15,080 --> 00:43:15,880
Does your stomach hurt?

1180
00:43:15,880 --> 00:43:16,920
I'm okay.

1181
00:43:17,720 --> 00:43:19,320
Let's see how your painting's
coming along.

1182
00:43:19,320 --> 00:43:20,720
I'm almost done.

1183
00:43:20,720 --> 00:43:22,280
But I've made such a mess.

1184
00:43:24,200 --> 00:43:25,840
I'm cleaning up the battlefield.

1185
00:43:27,860 --> 00:43:29,000
Let's see yours.

1186
00:43:30,440 --> 00:43:31,240
What do you think?

1187
00:43:32,760 --> 00:43:34,600
I think yours looks better than mine.

1188
00:43:34,600 --> 00:43:35,620
What looks better?

1189
00:43:35,620 --> 00:43:36,880
(Eager for praise)
What exactly?

1190
00:43:36,880 --> 00:43:39,720
The way you blended the colors

1191
00:43:39,720 --> 00:43:40,800
looks more natural than mine.

1192
00:43:40,800 --> 00:43:41,700
Especially here.

1193
00:43:41,700 --> 00:43:42,660
(Genuine praise)

1194
00:43:42,840 --> 00:43:43,840
Where the colors meet.

1195
00:43:43,840 --> 00:43:45,520
(Detailed compliments)
And those little yellow stars.

1196
00:43:47,080 --> 00:43:48,240
And these clouds.

1197
00:43:48,240 --> 00:43:49,600
You used this

1198
00:43:49,600 --> 00:43:50,920
outlining technique.

1199
00:43:52,800 --> 00:43:54,360
They really stand out.

1200
00:43:54,360 --> 00:43:55,320
It's unique.

1201
00:43:56,640 --> 00:43:57,480
Pretty good, right?

1202
00:43:57,480 --> 00:43:57,920
Yeah.

1203
00:43:57,920 --> 00:43:59,120
A master of color.

1204
00:44:00,020 --> 00:44:01,280
(Nods)

1205
00:44:01,280 --> 00:44:03,440
So what's the idea behind your painting?

1206
00:44:05,200 --> 00:44:06,680
First, this yellow dress

1207
00:44:06,680 --> 00:44:09,320
is what you're wearing today.

1208
00:44:09,320 --> 00:44:10,320
And you've worn

1209
00:44:10,320 --> 00:44:12,360
yellow dresses a lot before.

1210
00:44:12,840 --> 00:44:15,640
Those moments really stuck with me.

1211
00:44:18,400 --> 00:44:20,480
This really looks like me!

1212
00:44:21,220 --> 00:44:22,640
(Kaiyi, drawn by Yiheng)

1213
00:44:22,640 --> 00:44:23,600
And the background

1214
00:44:23,600 --> 00:44:25,480
is the view we've seen together most.

1215
00:44:25,880 --> 00:44:26,520
So pretty!

1216
00:44:26,520 --> 00:44:27,840
Our first sunset together.

1217
00:44:27,840 --> 00:44:28,660
Yeah.

1218
00:44:28,680 --> 00:44:30,560
This is gorgeous!

1219
00:44:35,520 --> 00:44:36,480
It's really beautiful.

1220
00:44:36,480 --> 00:44:37,680
Really?

1221
00:44:39,160 --> 00:44:40,480
So beautiful.

1222
00:44:45,440 --> 00:44:47,960
Come on, it's time to eat.

1223
00:44:48,400 --> 00:44:49,920
Right here?

1224
00:44:49,920 --> 00:44:50,720
Yeah.

1225
00:44:51,120 --> 00:44:53,280
This really feels like the Signal House.

1226
00:44:56,720 --> 00:44:58,840
The hot pot we missed out on that day!

1227
00:44:58,840 --> 00:45:01,260
(Monet's Garden)

1228
00:45:01,680 --> 00:45:03,790
(Snail noodle hot pot prepared by Yiheng)
This half is snail noodle broth.

1229
00:45:05,720 --> 00:45:08,120
I just remembered you
asked me the other day

1230
00:45:08,120 --> 00:45:10,120
if I'd ever had snail noodle hot pot.

1231
00:45:10,120 --> 00:45:10,940
(Surprised)
I said no!

1232
00:45:11,600 --> 00:45:12,400
Yeah.

1233
00:45:12,840 --> 00:45:14,280
(Signal House)
Wanna try snail noodles?

1234
00:45:14,280 --> 00:45:15,760
Sure. I like them.

1235
00:45:20,480 --> 00:45:21,520
So many pictures!

1236
00:45:22,380 --> 00:45:23,680
Even the old ones.

1237
00:45:24,100 --> 00:45:26,520
(Photo wall prepared by Yiheng)

1238
00:45:26,520 --> 00:45:27,520
They're so pretty.

1239
00:45:30,400 --> 00:45:32,400
These are all great!

1240
00:45:33,560 --> 00:45:35,560
This is the one you took of me.

1241
00:45:35,560 --> 00:45:37,120
Both of these look so good!

1242
00:45:40,800 --> 00:45:43,080
When did you take this, Cao Yiheng?

1243
00:45:43,840 --> 00:45:45,000
Does this belong here?

1244
00:45:45,000 --> 00:45:46,320
Why'd you include this one?

1245
00:45:46,340 --> 00:45:47,640
(Their first photo together
after leaving the Signal House)

1246
00:45:47,640 --> 00:45:49,120
Wasn't this from the day we met up

1247
00:45:49,120 --> 00:45:50,120
in the car?

1248
00:45:51,120 --> 00:45:52,520
I'm taking all these home later.

1249
00:45:53,960 --> 00:45:55,040
This smells so good!

1250
00:45:55,040 --> 00:45:56,600
We're really indulging today!

1251
00:45:56,600 --> 00:45:57,380
There's more!

1252
00:46:06,040 --> 00:46:06,790
And our...

1253
00:46:08,620 --> 00:46:10,040
(Key to the stargazing room)
Stargazing room!

1254
00:46:10,040 --> 00:46:11,120
Yeah.

1255
00:46:11,120 --> 00:46:12,840
We've got the key
to the stargazing room!

1256
00:46:14,840 --> 00:46:15,320
Yeah.

1257
00:46:17,720 --> 00:46:20,040
We were the last
to use the stargazing room.

1258
00:46:21,150 --> 00:46:22,160
Let's sit down first.

1259
00:46:22,160 --> 00:46:22,960
Okay.

1260
00:46:26,600 --> 00:46:28,000
I just noticed that!

1261
00:46:28,020 --> 00:46:30,320
(Astronomical telescope)

1262
00:46:30,320 --> 00:46:32,240
When I first thought
about our one-month anniversary,

1263
00:46:32,240 --> 00:46:35,240
I wanted to recreate the stargazing room

1264
00:46:35,240 --> 00:46:37,320
by decorating this place.

1265
00:46:38,380 --> 00:46:39,920
(While painting)
I'm gonna use the bathroom.

1266
00:46:39,920 --> 00:46:40,680
Go ahead.

1267
00:46:40,680 --> 00:46:41,600
Take your time painting.

1268
00:46:45,300 --> 00:46:46,620
(Food prepared in advance)

1269
00:46:47,660 --> 00:46:49,020
(Adds snail noodle soup base)

1270
00:46:49,060 --> 00:46:51,460
(Prepares hot pot ingredients)

1271
00:46:51,540 --> 00:46:53,700
(Homemade snail noodle hot pot)

1272
00:46:55,460 --> 00:47:01,300
(Sets up the photo wall)

1273
00:47:02,100 --> 00:47:03,420
(Adds little decorations)

1274
00:47:03,460 --> 00:47:04,940
(Adjusts the telescope)

1275
00:47:19,120 --> 00:47:20,840
I think this
is even better than last time.

1276
00:47:22,290 --> 00:47:23,800
And our stargazing room

1277
00:47:23,800 --> 00:47:25,280
is different from everyone else's.

1278
00:47:25,720 --> 00:47:27,680
Yeah, it's one of a kind.

1279
00:47:33,560 --> 00:47:34,960
You put so much thought into this!

1280
00:47:35,520 --> 00:47:36,400
Really?

1281
00:47:36,400 --> 00:47:37,200
Yeah!

1282
00:47:52,640 --> 00:47:53,320
Let's eat!

1283
00:47:53,320 --> 00:47:53,830
Okay!

1284
00:47:55,320 --> 00:47:57,520
My first time
having snail noodle hot pot.

1285
00:48:00,800 --> 00:48:01,450
Have the fried egg.

1286
00:48:01,450 --> 00:48:01,990
(Serves her food)
Thanks!

1287
00:48:05,320 --> 00:48:06,240
So good!

1288
00:48:07,560 --> 00:48:09,200
So spicy! I haven't
had spicy food in ages.

1289
00:48:09,200 --> 00:48:10,600
Try this stinky tofu.

1290
00:48:11,200 --> 00:48:13,240
Heat it up
and let it soak in the broth.

1291
00:48:13,920 --> 00:48:14,720
Okay.

1292
00:48:15,840 --> 00:48:16,460
Careful, it's hot.

1293
00:48:20,160 --> 00:48:21,160
This is so good.

1294
00:48:22,640 --> 00:48:24,280
Vacations are the best.

1295
00:48:26,220 --> 00:48:28,380
(Looks up)

1296
00:48:30,360 --> 00:48:31,440
No stars tonight.

1297
00:48:34,040 --> 00:48:34,910
Let's see if it works.

1298
00:48:35,300 --> 00:48:36,800
(Takes her hand)

1299
00:48:36,800 --> 00:48:37,600
Let's go.

1300
00:48:38,920 --> 00:48:40,640
I see one. Right there.

1301
00:48:40,640 --> 00:48:41,120
Where?

1302
00:48:41,120 --> 00:48:41,640
Right there.

1303
00:48:42,880 --> 00:48:43,920
Over there.

1304
00:48:44,840 --> 00:48:45,920
Let me adjust it.

1305
00:48:45,920 --> 00:48:46,720
Okay.

1306
00:48:48,000 --> 00:48:50,320
I'm pretty sure...

1307
00:48:50,740 --> 00:48:53,180
(Looking at him)

1308
00:49:10,060 --> 00:49:12,700
(Capturing the moment)

1309
00:49:14,600 --> 00:49:15,240
Almost got it.

1310
00:49:15,240 --> 00:49:16,400
Here, you can sit and look.

1311
00:49:21,800 --> 00:49:23,950
I don't think we'll see it
if it's even a little off.

1312
00:49:23,950 --> 00:49:25,160
There are barely any stars.

1313
00:49:26,280 --> 00:49:27,880
I moved it closer to the center.

1314
00:49:32,960 --> 00:49:35,040
See that little circle? That's the star.

1315
00:49:35,760 --> 00:49:36,820
I can even see its cells.

1316
00:49:36,820 --> 00:49:38,660
(Teasing)

1317
00:49:39,160 --> 00:49:41,200
You can see cells on a star? Seriously?

1318
00:49:42,000 --> 00:49:43,200
Does that even make sense?

1319
00:49:44,240 --> 00:49:46,720
I don't think we can see any stars.

1320
00:49:58,670 --> 00:50:00,200
Look at the picture I just took of you.

1321
00:50:07,320 --> 00:50:08,270
A gift for me?

1322
00:50:09,220 --> 00:50:10,160
Go ahead, open it.

1323
00:50:11,240 --> 00:50:12,040
Okay.

1324
00:50:16,040 --> 00:50:16,960
They're so pretty.

1325
00:50:17,020 --> 00:50:17,680
(Special star-shaped earrings)

1326
00:50:17,680 --> 00:50:18,320
Star earrings?

1327
00:50:18,320 --> 00:50:19,640
Yep.

1328
00:50:22,800 --> 00:50:24,480
I was afraid we wouldn't see any stars.

1329
00:50:25,560 --> 00:50:27,000
So you brought me some stars?

1330
00:50:28,920 --> 00:50:30,360
They're so pretty.

1331
00:50:32,320 --> 00:50:33,440
Prettier than the ones up there.

1332
00:50:33,880 --> 00:50:34,840
Prettier than what?

1333
00:50:34,840 --> 00:50:36,160
The stars in the sky.

1334
00:50:36,160 --> 00:50:37,200
(Prettier than the stars above)

1335
00:50:37,200 --> 00:50:38,600
The stars in the sky.

1336
00:50:47,800 --> 00:50:48,640
So pretty.

1337
00:50:53,160 --> 00:50:54,360
Here, put them on for me.

1338
00:50:58,340 --> 00:51:00,460
(Laughs)

1339
00:51:03,440 --> 00:51:04,110
Hold still.

1340
00:51:05,200 --> 00:51:05,920
Got it.

1341
00:51:06,020 --> 00:51:06,730
Did it go through?

1342
00:51:06,730 --> 00:51:07,480
Yeah.

1343
00:51:08,000 --> 00:51:08,760
So good at this now?

1344
00:51:08,760 --> 00:51:10,000
Here, the other one.

1345
00:51:13,880 --> 00:51:14,840
Okay, done.

1346
00:51:14,840 --> 00:51:15,600
Good.

1347
00:51:15,860 --> 00:51:16,710
There, it's on.

1348
00:51:16,720 --> 00:51:17,600
Perfect!

1349
00:51:25,440 --> 00:51:26,240
Does it look good?

1350
00:51:27,560 --> 00:51:28,400
Yeah.

1351
00:51:41,120 --> 00:51:43,280
Better keep my gift safe.

1352
00:51:45,000 --> 00:51:46,000
Let me fan you a little.

1353
00:51:53,990 --> 00:51:56,380
Do you think we've changed a lot
this past month?

1354
00:51:58,760 --> 00:52:00,480
I mean, since we've been together.

1355
00:52:00,480 --> 00:52:02,160
I feel like...

1356
00:52:02,620 --> 00:52:04,040
I've changed quite a bit.

1357
00:52:06,360 --> 00:52:08,160
Do you think I've changed at all?

1358
00:52:11,000 --> 00:52:12,120
Me?

1359
00:52:15,280 --> 00:52:17,540
I do think you've changed...

1360
00:52:17,540 --> 00:52:19,320
(Tilts head)
quite a bit.

1361
00:52:19,880 --> 00:52:20,960
Like how?

1362
00:52:21,520 --> 00:52:23,480
You're a little more...

1363
00:52:23,480 --> 00:52:24,760
soft and girly.

1364
00:52:25,660 --> 00:52:27,040
What do you mean?

1365
00:52:30,960 --> 00:52:32,520
Before I came to the Signal House,

1366
00:52:32,520 --> 00:52:34,160
back when I was single,

1367
00:52:34,160 --> 00:52:37,000
I handled everything on my own.

1368
00:52:37,000 --> 00:52:38,720
I'd try to work things out

1369
00:52:38,720 --> 00:52:40,000
and find answers myself.

1370
00:52:40,000 --> 00:52:41,240
But now, I've learned to...

1371
00:52:41,240 --> 00:52:41,920
Lean on me?

1372
00:52:41,920 --> 00:52:43,000
Lean on you more.

1373
00:52:43,020 --> 00:52:47,900
(I've learned to lean on you more
since we got together)

1374
00:52:48,360 --> 00:52:50,080
That's because you treat me so well.

1375
00:52:51,000 --> 00:52:52,800
I actually like it when you lean on me.

1376
00:52:52,800 --> 00:52:53,280
Really?

1377
00:52:53,280 --> 00:52:54,440
I lean on you, too.

1378
00:53:06,720 --> 00:53:07,440
Let me get

1379
00:53:07,440 --> 00:53:09,080
what you asked me about this morning.

1380
00:53:09,080 --> 00:53:10,240
Actually, this afternoon.

1381
00:53:10,720 --> 00:53:11,800
What did I ask about?

1382
00:53:11,940 --> 00:53:12,860
(Earlier today)

1383
00:53:12,880 --> 00:53:14,480
You brought a letter, too?

1384
00:53:14,480 --> 00:53:15,080
Is that a letter?

1385
00:53:15,080 --> 00:53:15,880
I'm not telling.

1386
00:53:15,880 --> 00:53:17,200
I'll keep this over here.

1387
00:53:21,360 --> 00:53:22,240
This is for you.

1388
00:53:22,300 --> 00:53:23,000
(A letter prepared in advance)

1389
00:53:23,000 --> 00:53:24,080
Wait, it really is a letter?

1390
00:53:24,080 --> 00:53:25,160
It is.

1391
00:53:25,160 --> 00:53:26,560
I wrote it this morning.

1392
00:53:26,800 --> 00:53:29,080
I wanted to start a little tradition.

1393
00:53:29,080 --> 00:53:29,560
Oh my God.

1394
00:53:30,440 --> 00:53:31,120
It's so thick.

1395
00:53:33,000 --> 00:53:34,120
It's a love letter.

1396
00:53:34,390 --> 00:53:34,940
Oh my God.

1397
00:53:35,480 --> 00:53:36,590
Then I'll say yes.

1398
00:53:36,590 --> 00:53:39,120
(Then I'll say yes)

1399
00:53:39,120 --> 00:53:40,080
Come on.

1400
00:53:40,080 --> 00:53:41,680
Didn't you already say yes to me?

1401
00:53:41,940 --> 00:53:43,380
(Playful pinch)

1402
00:53:44,120 --> 00:53:45,520
Look how many pages there are.

1403
00:53:46,960 --> 00:53:48,640
I'll write you one every anniversary.

1404
00:53:48,660 --> 00:53:51,660
(A love letter for every anniversary)

1405
00:53:52,080 --> 00:53:52,830
Oh my God.

1406
00:53:57,080 --> 00:53:59,800
Hello, my dear boyfriend, Cao Yiheng.

1407
00:54:02,530 --> 00:54:05,360
Today marks our one-month anniversary.

1408
00:54:05,360 --> 00:54:07,360
Thank you for making me feel

1409
00:54:07,360 --> 00:54:09,640
so reassured and loved
these past 30 days.

1410
00:54:10,640 --> 00:54:11,920
After leaving the Signal House,

1411
00:54:11,920 --> 00:54:12,880
I realized that you're still

1412
00:54:12,880 --> 00:54:14,520
the same person you were there.

1413
00:54:14,520 --> 00:54:16,720
If anything, you're even better
than I imagined.

1414
00:54:18,560 --> 00:54:20,920
In a world where people come and go,

1415
00:54:20,920 --> 00:54:22,520
I'm so glad we found each other.

1416
00:54:22,960 --> 00:54:25,880
I hope I can always

1417
00:54:25,880 --> 00:54:28,560
be your never-ending paintbox,
adding color to your life.

1418
00:54:40,920 --> 00:54:42,840
As time goes by,

1419
00:54:42,840 --> 00:54:45,440
we may see more of each other's flaws.

1420
00:54:46,880 --> 00:54:48,600
But even then, I hope

1421
00:54:49,320 --> 00:54:51,260
we'll still love each other

1422
00:54:51,920 --> 00:54:52,960
the way we do now.

1423
00:55:02,380 --> 00:55:04,800
I'll treasure this letter.

1424
00:55:05,280 --> 00:55:06,600
Of course you have to.

1425
00:55:09,840 --> 00:55:11,200
You'd better keep it forever.

1426
00:55:11,200 --> 00:55:13,200
What I really want to say

1427
00:55:13,200 --> 00:55:15,280
is I hope we get to celebrate

1428
00:55:15,280 --> 00:55:17,160
many more anniversaries together.

1429
00:55:17,340 --> 00:55:21,700
(Here's to many more
anniversaries together)

1430
00:55:21,720 --> 00:55:22,720
And I hope you'll always

1431
00:55:23,600 --> 00:55:25,600
be happy, healthy, and safe.

1432
00:55:25,600 --> 00:55:30,340
(I hope you'll always be happy,
healthy, and safe)

1433
00:55:30,360 --> 00:55:32,840
I hope you stay happy and healthy, too.

1434
00:55:37,110 --> 00:55:37,870
Yeah.

1435
00:55:45,960 --> 00:55:48,040
What a memorable anniversary.

1436
00:55:48,040 --> 00:55:49,120
(An anniversary to remember)

1437
00:55:49,120 --> 00:55:51,160
One we'll never forget.

1438
00:55:51,160 --> 00:55:59,500
(An anniversary we'll never forget)

1439
00:56:00,400 --> 00:56:02,520
(Next episode)
I hope we have a great future together.

1440
00:56:02,520 --> 00:56:03,320
Of course we will.

1441
00:56:03,320 --> 00:56:04,960
Need to hurry up
and finish grad school already.

1442
00:56:04,960 --> 00:56:06,600
Let's make every day a happy one.

1443
00:56:07,200 --> 00:56:08,240
You be happy, too.

1444
00:56:13,000 --> 00:56:16,080
We could make a whole special
just about your voice.

1445
00:56:23,600 --> 00:56:24,580
You're giving off Queen Ka vibes.

1446
00:56:24,580 --> 00:56:25,140
(Unbothered queen)

1447
00:56:26,440 --> 00:56:27,160
Would you be okay

1448
00:56:27,160 --> 00:56:28,120
with this smaller one?

1449
00:56:28,280 --> 00:56:29,120
It's seriously good.

1450
00:56:29,960 --> 00:56:30,800
Yihang made this.

1451
00:56:30,800 --> 00:56:31,480
Give it a try.

1452
00:56:33,160 --> 00:56:33,760
So good.

1453
00:56:33,760 --> 00:56:35,280
It's as good as the Thai restaurant's.

1454
00:56:35,280 --> 00:56:36,400
Yeah, even better than that Thai place.

1455
00:56:36,700 --> 00:56:37,080
(Smiles)

1456
00:56:37,080 --> 00:56:37,920
Look at that smile.

1457
00:56:38,840 --> 00:56:40,680
So, when are you planning to visit

1458
00:56:40,680 --> 00:56:41,880
their hometown in Tieling?

1459
00:56:41,880 --> 00:56:42,800
(Looks over)
Like, going for a proper visit.

1460
00:56:42,800 --> 00:56:43,480
Do you want to go alone

1461
00:56:43,480 --> 00:56:44,400
or with me?

1462
00:56:44,400 --> 00:56:45,120
Like, go together?

1463
00:57:00,480 --> 00:57:03,200
♪Morning steam rises
from breakfast stalls♪

1464
00:57:03,200 --> 00:57:05,800
♪Packed subway cars,
barely room to breathe♪

1465
00:57:05,800 --> 00:57:10,000
♪Still half asleep, another day begins♪

1466
00:57:11,160 --> 00:57:13,880
♪The city glows beneath the towers♪

1467
00:57:13,880 --> 00:57:16,520
♪Somewhere beyond the clouds,
a sweet little date awaits♪

1468
00:57:16,520 --> 00:57:20,600
♪But first,
there are endless meetings to survive♪

1469
00:57:21,320 --> 00:57:22,720
♪Even if the fairy tale
only lasts a day♪

1470
00:57:22,720 --> 00:57:24,040
♪I'll still give it everything I have♪

1471
00:57:24,040 --> 00:57:25,360
♪Love out loud♪

1472
00:57:25,360 --> 00:57:26,760
♪Don't let this summer slip away♪

1473
00:57:26,760 --> 00:57:28,000
♪Cupid's arrow is already on its way♪

1474
00:57:28,000 --> 00:57:29,400
♪Don't act like you didn't see it♪

1475
00:57:29,400 --> 00:57:32,360
♪Just be a little braver♪

1476
00:57:32,360 --> 00:57:33,600
♪Keep moving♪

1477
00:57:33,720 --> 00:57:35,200
♪Keep moving♪

1478
00:57:35,200 --> 00:57:38,560
♪There's a little spark shining
in your eyes♪

1479
00:57:40,920 --> 00:57:43,280
♪That's the signal
of a heart coming alive♪

1480
00:57:53,720 --> 00:57:56,520
♪Keep moving♪

1481
00:57:56,520 --> 00:57:59,160
♪Life can be complicated,
yet beautifully simple♪

1482
00:57:59,160 --> 00:58:01,800
♪Go discover♪

1483
00:58:01,800 --> 00:58:04,480
♪That heartbeat you've been longing
to let out♪

1484
00:58:04,480 --> 00:58:07,160
♪Come closer♪

1485
00:58:07,160 --> 00:58:10,560
♪There's a little spark shining
in your eyes♪

1486
00:58:13,000 --> 00:58:15,800
♪That's the signal
of a heart coming alive♪
